  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Framework Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve dived into the framework\'s needs, specifically focusing on the full-stack architecture. The instructions are clear: an Express server in `server.ts` with `vite.middlewares` for development and distinct build steps for deployment. This separation is crucial, and I\'m noting the explicit prohibition of combining Express with `vite.config.ts`. Now, let\'s explore how the existing structure aligns with these specs.\n\n\n**Analyzing Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on package dependencies, specifically the discrepancy in the `@google/genai` version. The framework requires >= 2.25.0, but the current version could be older. I\'m planning to upgrade using `install_applet_package`. Also, I\'m noting the dev and start scripts: `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\": \"NODE_ENV=production tsx server.ts\"` in `package.json`. Furthermore, I\'m looking at math and PDF rendering.\n\n\n"
