  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Architecture Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the server architecture and full-stack integration, specifically the use of `server.ts` with Express and `vite.middlewares` for backend routes. The instructions clearly indicate using this approach in development, which will be the focus of the current review.\n\n\n**Designing Backend Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now diving into the backend endpoint design. The plan is to create specific routes, starting with `/api/tutor/chat` and `/api/roadmap/generate`. I need to define the inputs, model specifications (like `\'gemini-3.8-flash\'`), and expected outputs for each endpoint. The tutor endpoint will feature detailed concept explanations, follow-up prompts, and interactive quizzes. The roadmap endpoint requires generating study roadmaps.\n\n\n**Defining Roadmap Outputs**\n\nI\'ve been working on the `/api/roadmap/generate` endpoint, and I\'m fleshing out the response structure. It will return a structured study plan, with details like roadmap title, summary, total estimated hours, and daily tasks. Each day will include a number, date, theme, and an array of tasks with IDs, titles, durations, topics, subtopics, and learning objectives, as well as a tutor prompt for each. A completion status will also be provided.\n\n\n**Structuring Assessment Details**\n\nI\'m now outlining the structure for the assessment data that will feed into the tutor functionality. This includes the paper summary, difficulty distribution, detailed topic breakdown with priorities, actionable advice, and individual question details. The data model also includes strategic revision plan recommendations, which will inform the overall user experience. I\'m focusing on organizing this structured output with an eye towards efficiency and user comprehension.\n\n\n"
