    model_api_content_id: "DtXlat7iA-DG-sAPuMyKwQ4"
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user requirements for the client-side experience. The core concept is \"Study Flow: Your Studies, Your Pace, Your Success.\" It\'s an all-in-one study companion designed to simplify complex concepts and facilitate exam preparation for students. I\'m focusing on how to translate these needs into a seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Scope**\n\nI\'m now outlining key functionalities within the app, specifically focusing on the user\'s ability to organise their study schedules and manage time effectively. The dashboard will now include a welcome message with a streak, and current focus time, along with a motivational quote. Also, an overview of study activity, and quick access cards. I\'m prioritizing the AI Tutor section, which will use a conversational chat interface with subject and grade level selectors.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Assessments**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive multiple-choice assessment feature. Students will select answers with immediate, colored feedback, score tracking, and visual celebrations. I\'m focusing on pre-loaded topic prompts, and I\'m adding support for text, images, and documents. I\'m also planning the study roadmap, including chapter uploads, subject inputs, and AI-generated daily schedules.\n\n\n**Integrating New Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features to enhance the \"Study Flow\" app. I\'m adding a progress indicator to show completed vs. total hours. There is a \'Start Learning\' button, that will pre-fill the AI Tutor with the current task\'s prompt, and I\'m adding the ability to save and switch between study roadmaps. Now, I\'m developing the paper analyzer with PDF and image upload for preloaded exam papers, providing detailed analysis with difficulty distribution, and strategic revision timelines.\n\n\n**Implementing Time Management Tools**\n\nI\'m now implementing time management tools, including Pomodoro timers with preset and custom durations and a stopwatch, both with start/pause/reset controls. These timers will use a visual circular ring progress indicator, sound alerts via Web Audio API, and automatically log sessions in the Progress Dashboard. I\'m also adding background ambient study sounds synthesized via the Web Audio API.\n\n**Expanding Progress Tracking**\n\nI\'m expanding the progress tracking feature to include study time statistics, such as daily and weekly hours, focus sessions, and Pomodoro streaks. I\'m tracking completed roadmaps, task completion rates, assessment results with average scores and a topic mastery matrix, and creating a learning activity log with recent actions and achievements, along with a printable/exportable study report or data reset.\n\n\n**Adding Note Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing note-taking features, with the ability to create, edit, delete, and search notes. I\'m organising notes by subject and tags, and adding a \"Save from AI Tutor\" button for direct note saving. A formula bank and markdown preview are also on the roadmap. I\'m focusing on the dark aesthetic with violet accents, and incorporating subtle glassmorphism for visual appeal.\n\nI\'m also working on local storage persistence to save all data. Currently, I\'m building a clean `types` and `storage` module.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_148562"
      name: "write_to_file"
