 potential, electrochemical gradient\"],\"taskType\":\"formula-memorization\",\"title\":\"Bioenergetics Key Terminology & Concepts\",\"topic\":\"Terminology & Formulas\",\"tutorPrompt\":\"Quiz me on the fundamental terms and gradients involved in mitochondrial ATP generation.\"}],\"theme\":\"The Proton Motive Force\",\"title\":\"Electron Transport and Electrochemical Gradients\"},{\"dayNumber\":3,\"estimatedMinutes\":45,\"phase\":\"Mastery\",\"tasks\":[{\"durationMinutes\":25,\"id\":\"day3-task1\",\"learningObjectives\":[\"Explain the rotary catalytic mechanism of ATP Synthase (F0 and F1 subunits)\",\"Describe how proton flux drives ATP phosphorylation from ADP + Pi\"],\"taskType\":\"theory\",\"title\":\"Mechanism of ATP Synthase Rotary Motor\",\"topic\":\"ATP Synthase Mechanism\",\"tutorPrompt\":\"Teach me the rotary motor mechanism of ATP Synthase, focusing on the roles of the F0 rotor subunit in the membrane and the F1 catalytic headpiece in the matrix.\"},{\"durationMinutes\":20,\"id\":\"day3-task2\",\"learningObjectives\":[\"Solve conceptual exam questions regarding uncouplers (e.g., DNP) and respiratory inhibitors (e.g., cyanide)\"],\"taskType\":\"problem-solving\",\"title\":\"Practice Scenarios: Inhibitors and Transport Uncouplers\",\"topic\":\"Cell Bio Problem-Solving\",\"tutorPrompt\":\"Give me 2 classic exam scenario questions on what happens to ATP yield and oxygen consumption when mitochondrial membrane transport is disrupted or uncoupled.\"}],\"theme\":\"ATP Synthesis & Exam Problem Solving\",\"title\":\"ATP Synthase Function & Clinical/Exam Applications\"}],\"keyMilestones\":[\"Understand mitochondrial compartmentalization and transport across membranes\",\"Master the generation of the proton electrochemical gradient\",\"Comprehend the rotary mechanism of ATP synthase and solve scenario-based questions\"],\"roadmapTitle\":\"Cell Biology: Mitochondria, ATP Synthase & Membrane Transport Mastery Plan\",\"subject\":\"Cell Biology\",\"summary\":\"A focused 