    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s request. My priority is understanding the need to rectify the AI Tutor\'s error handling within the Study Flow app. Specifically, I\'ve identified the need to properly manage temporary 503 errors.\n\n\n**Refining the Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing automatic retries with exponential backoff and jitter for 503 errors, limiting it to three attempts. I\'m also addressing the issue of duplicate responses. I\'m working to provide a more user-friendly UI, instead of displaying the raw JSON, and the inclusion of a \"Retry\" button. I\'m focused on preserving the student\'s question, so they do not have to type it again. Further, I\'m defining specific messages for other error codes.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Model Alternatives**\n\nI\'m now determining fallback models for when the primary is overloaded or unavailable. I\'m focusing on preserving all existing app functionality while improving error handling. The UI should display friendly messages with a retry button instead of the raw JSON. I need to test all implemented error-handling features with simulated 503 errors and other failures.\n\n\n"
