    thinking: "**Analyzing the Error Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the error message display, specifically lines 507-516. The conditional rendering using `errorMsg` seems straightforward, but I\'m examining the styling: the background color, border, text color, and overall layout. The goal is to fully understand its visual presentation, and how it impacts the user.\n\n\n**Addressing the Retry Mechanism**\n\nI\'ve uncovered critical flaws in the retry mechanism related to error handling. Specifically, pressing \'Retry\' was not sending any new information because the input field was immediately cleared. Moreover, duplicate messages were being appended to the session. I\'m now focusing on how to prevent these duplicates, and implement the requested 503 error handling with automatic retries and jitter.\n\n\n**Refining the Error Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI improvements for error handling. Instead of raw JSON, I\'ll display user-friendly messages for different error codes. Specifically, I\'m focusing on preserving the student\'s original question in the chat upon failure, and implementing a \"Retry\" button that resends the original request. The plan includes specific messages for 429, 401/403, and network errors. I am trying to ensure no duplicate messages get created on retry attempts.\n\n\n**Evaluating Model Alternatives**\n\nI\'m now investigating model failover strategies for 503 errors. I\'ve confirmed that `\'gemini-3.8-flash\'` is the primary model, and I\'m aware of the deprecated models. I will look at `\'gemini-flash-latest\'` and `\'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'` as potential free alternatives if the primary experiences high demand after retries with jitter. I\'m planning tests with simulated 503 and 429 errors.\n\n\n**Designing the Server-Side Solution**\n\nI\'m architecting the server-side solution (`server.ts`) now. I am working on a `parseGeminiError` helper to parse error codes and messages from the Gemini API and provide user-friendly messages for 503, 429, 401, network, and unknown errors. I am also planning the `generateContentWithSmartRetry` function to handle the primary model and retries.\n\n\n**Implementing Model Failover**\n\nI\'m now integrating the model failover strategy. I\'m focusing on the retry logic, specifically implementing three attempts with exponential backoff and jitter for the primary model, `\'gemini-3.8-flash\'`. If all retries fail, I\'ll switch to the secondary model, `\'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'`. If that also fails, I\'ll return a structured error response with status 503 and a user-friendly message. Furthermore, I will create standardized JSON error responses across the `/api` routes.\n\n\n**Defining Error State Management**\n\nI\'m now designing the error state tracking mechanism on the client-side using `TutorErrorState`. I\'m going beyond a simple error string; I\'m implementing a structured approach with a code and a message. I\'m focusing on preserving the user\'s input, the attachments, and assessment status, ensuring that these are not lost in case of errors.\n\n\n**Refining the Retry Behavior**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed retry logic. I\'m focusing on ensuring the student\'s input isn\'t lost during retries. I\'m storing `pendingRetryAction` details. I am also planning the error banner styling to look like a notification card, below the message in the chat stream with an alert icon, clear explanation and a retry button that won\'t duplicate the message in the chat history. I am also verifying that if the student was typing another message, that this is preserved during retries.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Display States**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the different error display states. I\'ll need distinct cards for 503/Busy (amber/violet), 429/Rate Limit (amber), 401/403/Auth (rose), and Network errors (slate/rose). Each will have a specific message and \"Retry\" button. I\'m making sure to ensure that if a student begins typing while another request is active, that this new request is handled correctly.\n\n\n**Defining Error UI Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI details for each error type, with specific messages and retry buttons. I\'ll preserve student questions across retries and ensure the error banner follows a notification card style. I\'m testing with simulated 503 and 429 responses. My plan is to maintain all existing features and avoid inventing model names or using paid services. I will also make sure that student\'s subsequent input is preserved during an active retry process.\n\n\n"
