    thinking: "**Defining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the error parsing and retry logic within `server.ts`. I\'m defining a structured `ParsedErrorInfo` interface to categorize Gemini errors based on status codes and specific error codes like \"MODEL_BUSY_503\" or \"USAGE_LIMIT_429\". My goal is to create robust, efficient handling for common errors.\n\n\n**Refining Error Parsing**\n\nI\'ve been refining the `parseGeminiError` function. I\'m focusing on robustly parsing Gemini errors, including those nested in JSON structures. I\'m extracting error codes, status texts, and inner messages to generate a structured `ParsedErrorInfo` object, with friendly and technical descriptions. I\'m aiming for resilience to variations in error formatting, including nested JSON.\n\n\n**Categorizing Error Conditions**\n\nI\'m now implementing detailed error condition categorization. I\'m focusing specifically on crafting error responses for 503 and 429 status codes, considering various scenarios like \"high demand,\" \"overloaded,\" \"quota,\" and \"usage limit\" messages within the error details. I\'m building out distinct `ParsedErrorInfo` structures to cover both scenarios, with tailored friendly and technical messages.\n\n\n**Classifying Authentication Issues**\n\nI\'m now integrating authentication and network error handling within the `parseGeminiError` function. I\'ve added specific checks for 401 and 403 errors, along with related status texts and error strings like \'API\\_KEY\\_INVALID\'. I\'m also including \'network\' and connectivity errors, mapping these to meaningful `ParsedErrorInfo` structures. I\'m focusing on crafting detailed responses.\n\n\n**Defining Fallback Strategies**\n\nI\'m now implementing a default fallback for unhandled errors within `parseGeminiError`, using a 500 status code and a generic message. I\'m focusing on providing concise technical details from the error message. I\'m moving on to `generateContentWithSmartRetry`, aiming to implement automated retries with exponential backoff and random delays, up to three attempts. I\'ll also inspect the Gemini model for overload conditions and intelligently switch to a supported alternative, like \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\', if necessary.\n\n\n**Implementing Retry Logic**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the retry logic with exponential backoff for the \'gemini-3.8-flash\' model. Specifically, I\'m working with the exponential delay calculation, incorporating a random jitter for added robustness. The goal is to achieve reliable error handling for transient issues, switching to the \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\' fallback after all retry attempts fail. I\'m also planning to incorporate a mechanism to simulate errors to test the workflow, to ensure that retries are working as expected.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_301166"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Implement parseGeminiError, exponential backoff with jitter, and supported fallback model in server.ts\", \"EndLine\":60, \"Instruction\":\"Replace generateContentWithRetry with smart retry and model fallback\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"// Structured Gemini error info\\ninterface ParsedErrorInfo {\\n  statusCode: number;\\n  errorCode: \'MODEL_BUSY_503\' | \'USAGE_LIMIT_429\' | \'AUTH_ERROR_401\' | \'NETWORK_ERROR\' | \'SERVICE_ERROR\';\\n  friendlyMessage: string;\\n  technicalDetails?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport function parseGeminiError(error: any): ParsedErrorInfo {\\n  const errStr = typeof error === \'string\' ? error : (error?.message || JSON.stringify(error) || \'\');\\n  \\n  let code = error?.status || error?.code;\\n  let statusText = error?.statusText || \'\';\\n  let innerMsg = error?.message || \'\';\\n\\n  try {\\n    const jsonMatch = errStr.match(/\\\\{[\\\\s\\\\S]*\\\"error\\\"[\\\\s\\\\S]*\\\\}/);\\n    if (jsonMatch) {\\n      const parsed = JSON.parse(jsonMatch[0]);\\n      if (parsed?.error) {\\n        if (parsed.error.code) code = parsed.error.code;\\n        if (parsed.error.status) statusText = parsed.error.status;\\n        if (parsed.error.message) innerMsg = parsed.error.message;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    // ignore json parse error\\n  }\\n\\n  // 1. 503 / Service Unavailable / High demand\\n  if (\\n    code === 503 ||\\n    statusText === \'UNAVAILABLE\' ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'503\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'high demand\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'overloaded\') ||\\n    innerMsg.includes(\'high demand\')\\n  ) {\\n    return {\\n      statusCode: 503,\\n      errorCode: \'MODEL_BUSY_503\',\\n      friendlyMessage: \'Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment.\',\\n      technicalDetails: innerMsg || \'Model experiencing high demand (503 UNAVAILABLE)\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. 429 / Resource Exhausted / Quota\\n  if (\\n    code === 429 ||\\n    statusText === \'RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\' ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'429\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'quota\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'usage limit\')\\n  ) {\\n    return {\\n      statusCode: 429,\\n      errorCode: \'USAGE_LIMIT_429\',\\n      friendlyMessage: \'The usage limit has been reached. Please wait a moment before trying again.\',\\n      technicalDetails: innerMsg || \'API rate limit reached (429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED)\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 3. 401 / 403 / Authentication\\n  if (\\n    code === 401 ||\\n    code === 403 ||\\n    statusText === \'PERMISSION_DENIED\' ||\\n    statusText === \'UNAUTHENTICATED\' ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'401\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'403\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'API_KEY_INVALID\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'PERMISSION_DENIED\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'authentication\')\\n  ) {\\n    return {\\n      statusCode: 401,\\n      errorCode: \'AUTH_ERROR_401\',\\n      friendlyMessage: \'API authentication needs attention. Please verify your API key in Settings > Secrets.\',\\n      technicalDetails: innerMsg || \'Authentication failed (401/403)\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 4. Network / Connectivity\\n  if (\\n    errStr.includes(\'ECONNRESET\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'ENOTFOUND\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'ETIMEDOUT\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'fetch failed\') ||\\n    errStr.includes(\'network\')\\n  ) {\\n    return {\\n      statusCode: 502,\\n      errorCode: \'NETWORK_ERROR\',\\n      friendlyMessage: \'Connection to the AI service failed. Please check your network connection and try again.\',\\n      technicalDetails: innerMsg || \'Network connection failed\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    statusCode: 500,\\n    errorCode: \'SERVICE_ERROR\',\\n    friendlyMessage: \'Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment.\',\\n    technicalDetails: innerMsg || errStr.slice(0, 150),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// Supported active models from @google/genai guidelines\\nconst PRIMARY_MODEL = \'gemini-3.8-flash\';\\nconst FALLBACK_MODEL = \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\';\\n\\n// Exponential backoff with jitter and supported model fallback\\nasync function generateContentWithSmartRetry(\\n  ai: GoogleGenAI, \\n  params: any, \\n  maxRetries = 3\\n): Promise<{ response: any; modelUsed: string; retriesDone: number }> {\\n  let lastError: any = null;\\n  let modelToUse = params.model || PRIMARY_MODEL;\\n\\n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\\n    try {\\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n        ...params,\\n        model: modelToUse,\\n      });\\n      return { response, modelUsed: modelToUse, retriesDone: attempt - 1 };\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      lastError = err;\\n      const parsed = parseGeminiError(err);\\n\\n      // Check if transient 503 or network error that benefits from exponential retry\\n      const isTransient = parsed.statusCode === 503 || parsed.errorCode === \'NETWORK_ERROR\';\\n\\n      if (isTransient && attempt < maxRetries) {\\n        // Exponential backoff with small random jitter (150ms - 450ms)\\n        const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random() * 300) + 150;\\n        const delay = Math.pow(2, attempt - 1) * 1000 + jitter; // ~1.2s, ~2.3s\\n        console.warn(`[AI Service] Attempt ${attempt}/${maxRetries} failed (${parsed.errorCode}). Retrying in ${delay}ms with jitter...`);\\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n\\n      // If primary model failed all attempts with 503 high demand, try the supported fallback model\\n      if (isTransient && modelToUse === PRIMARY_MODEL && attempt === maxRetries) {\\n        console.warn(`[AI Service] ${PRIMARY_MODEL} busy after ${maxRetries} attempts. Switching to supported alternative model ${FALLBACK_MODEL}...`);\\n        try {\\n          const fallbackResponse = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n            ...params,\\n            model: FALLBACK_MODEL,\\n          });\\n          return { response: fallbackResponse, modelUsed: FALLBACK_MODEL, retriesDone: maxRetries };\\n        } catch (fallbackErr: any) {\\n          console.error(`[AI Service] Fallback model ${FALLBACK_MODEL} also failed:`, fallbackErr);\\n          lastError = fallbackErr;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      throw err;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  throw lastError;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":34, \"TargetContent\":\"// Retry helper for handling transient 503/429 upstream hiccups\\nasync function generateContentWithRetry(ai: GoogleGenAI, params: any, maxRetries = 3): Promise<any> {\\n  let lastError: any = null;\\n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\\n    try {\\n      return await ai.models.generateContent(params);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      lastError = err;\\n      const isTransient = \\n        err?.status === 503 || \\n        err?.message?.includes(\'503\') || \\n        err?.message?.includes(\'high demand\') ||\\n        err?.message?.includes(\'RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\') ||\\n        err?.status === 429;\\n\\n      if (isTransient && attempt < maxRetries) {\\n        const delay = attempt * 1200;\\n        console.warn(`Gemini call transient error (attempt ${attempt}/${maxRetries}), retrying in ${delay}ms...`);\\n        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      throw err;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  throw lastError;\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating server.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Implement parseGeminiError and smart retry with model fallback\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\2077\n\2047\001i\024}\023C\357\034U\210\327\351\2769\332\"\373o\037n\346RD\274\364\323~t\347\275\034\262a`\363T\357\324\245\362\360\221&\210]\345\223!\1775u\'\377\023\362\237\t\372,\t\220W\030DM\230&b\251\372!b\275\357\250\rW\303\244\344\r \003\352u\024\374_\207\267\320\251v>{\327\220\'}\305\2444\245\246g\234\310f}\304\235\317,}\364\312P:/\252\274\324\334\340\220R\277\257\244a\205\233\250\353\253\\\363\331\033`\230\025\373\271&!\302\370`\243\035&S\241$\257\204\376\376p\303\227\351\320@\367\307\334\312#\310\317@r\022J\376\214<E\272+\257~\262\302\253;\334\250\370W\221\035\025\000\344l7\363p\342F\347T\343\016\\\270\370\037\037f\267\234\342 \006{\256GWkqx\3649\276\217\272\377\355\235G2\231O\202g\204z\247\v\264n\031\254\v\024\246\037-p\001\031\t\315\263f\323\0027\351\354\021\206\313\025\371\247[4Oi\034\355\224w\370\221Za\316\304\341\017\3030\241i\321\224\351\237\t\372a>\207\216\277\261\233x\3526\177_\006\204\020A\212Fs\235\214\022\261\027}Z\323\334\fxH:l\2129z]\222J\220wU\3367.\336X\271$\327s\005\350sS\026$\336A\373y\303\347\343\242\033\270\202R8\237\201\340a\315\001\266\211\342 Z\251IePJrD\361\307\241\231\342\231\273mO\361\366Q\253\036f\240)w\023\316\325\250\343|w-4V<\025/pA\322\236\247k\311$\363\304\356\334gj\351\367*\0171B\316\017\002UC;\314\341\322u\202\257\237\213\336\201\371$\204?\234\233\fr\331\372\275J\251\336\324\313\037)\341\016\036\b\200\360+\272cb\020\312\360\343\203\317\233\006\244\255\316\262\302/4\351\203\336\032\000S\a\375Ob\tD\271\250\314Z\374\263\204\2444\a\344\364\036F\272S\3434\322AB\225\353\330\001\274\251\303\375/H\b\361\313\027\300\255\267\n\247ru\253\367-_\257\315\213\017\"\037\265\036ZJ\303\2111\210\251\260l^\360O\237\337D\341\002M0\231du\263\177\263\017)D\254\030\322L\350\242]hs\277\212\261\326\177{\367\223\002\326\371O\221\344V\3315\231F\205P\233V\226-\346#6c\370L\242\257!3$M\323>\005\310\361\245\021\202\222\317vdA\324W\254\002\257.\177t\353\303_\233\023\204\303\373,\256\303\366*>\251\211K\360\033\320^\276+\216~a