  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Server Code**\n\nI\'m currently focused on updating `server.ts` to include error simulation capabilities, specifically the `/api/tutor/chat` endpoint. I\'m adding support for a `simulateError` header to the request to allow for targeted testing of error handling. This is the initial step; the remaining endpoints will follow.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve refined the error simulation logic. Based on the `simulateError` header or body parameter, I\'m now throwing specific errors (503, 429, 401) with detailed JSON messages, simulating real-world API failures. The catch block parses Gemini errors and returns a structured response with status codes, error codes, and user-friendly messages for robust error management.\n\n\n"
