    thinking: "**Adding New Components**\n\nI\'m currently updating `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`. My focus now is on importing several new icons from \'lucide-react\': `RotateCcw`, `ShieldAlert`, `AlertCircle`, `Clock`, and `FlaskConical`. I\'m also in the process of defining `TutorErrorState`.\n\n\n**Defining Error States**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining `TutorErrorState` which includes fields for `message`, `errorCode`, `statusCode`, and others to capture detailed error information. I\'m also implementing state management for the `activeError` with `useState` and setting up a `simulatedErrorMode` for testing. I\'m handling error responses in the `sendMessage` function and extracting error details like friendly messages and error codes from the response. I\'m also checking for specific error statuses such as 503 and 429 and providing user-friendly messages for these cases.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the error handling logic within the `catch` block. I\'m ensuring that a user-friendly message is displayed even if the error message is not a standard string or starts with a JSON-like structure. I\'m also setting a default status code of 502 for network errors. Further, I\'ve incorporated checks to handle specific error codes, setting the `friendlyMsg` and `code` variables appropriately based on the response status, such as \"USAGE_LIMIT_429,\" and other authentication errors.\n\n\n**Implementing Retry Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `handleRetry` function, which checks for an `activeError`, resends the current session messages without duplication, appends the AI response, and clears the `activeError`. I\'ve also focused on the UI display for `activeError`, rendering a styled card above the messages end reference. Specific messages and retry functionality are being implemented based on error codes like 503, 429, 401/403, and network errors, including displaying the preserved user question.\n\n\n"
