  planner_response {
    response: "### Improvements Implemented\n\n1. **Automatic Retries with Exponential Backoff & Jitter**\n   - Implemented `generateContentWithSmartRetry` on the server with a maximum of 3 retry attempts for transient `503 Service Unavailable` and network errors.\n   - Added randomized jitter delays (150ms\342\200\223450ms) between exponential intervals (`~1.2s`, `~2.3s`) to prevent synchronization thundering herds during upstream demand spikes.\n\n2. **Clean, User-Friendly UI (No Raw JSON)**\n   - Replaced raw JSON displays with styled notification banners.\n   - For temporary 503 errors, the UI displays:\n     > **\"Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment.\"**\n   - Paired with an immediate, prominent **Retry Question** button and status indicator.\n\n3. **Question Preservation & Duplicate Prevention**\n   - When a request fails, the student\'s question and any attachments remain saved in the conversation history and local storage.\n   - The student does not have to retype their question.\n   - Clicking **Retry Question** re-evaluates the existing pending message without appending duplicate messages or polluting the conversation history.\n\n4. **Specific Error Classification**\n   - **503 (High Demand / Unavailable):** Explains that the model is temporarily busy, with exponential retries and an instant retry button.\n   - **429 (Usage Limit):** Explains that the usage limit has been reached and prompts the student to wait a moment before retrying.\n   - **401 / 403 (Authentication):** Informs the user that API authentication requires attention in *Settings > Secrets*.\n   - **Network Failures:** Informs the student that the connection to the AI service failed and provides a retry option.\n\n5. **Supported Model Fallback**\n   - Configured `gemini-3.8-flash` as primary.\n   - If the primary model encounters repeated 503 high-demand errors, the system automatically falls back to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, an active and supported standard model, without switching to paid services or using deprecated models.\n\n6. **Preservation of All Existing Features**\n   - Full conversational memory across multiple saved sessions.\n   - Standalone SVG conceptual diagram rendering and formula formatting.\n   - Interactive assessment quizzes and *\"Save to My Notes\"* functionality.\n   - Integration with the AI Study Roadmap and Exam Paper Analyzer.\n\n7. **Interactive Error Simulation Testing**\n   - Added a testing mode selector in the AI Tutor header (`Live AI`, `Test 503`, `Test 429`, `Test 401`, `Test Network Error`) to verify the error card, question preservation, and retry workflows directly."
