  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the user\'s needs for the Study Flow application. My primary focus is on identifying three key problem areas. First, I am investigating how to significantly improve the AI response speed, specifically looking into why `/api/tutor/chat` waits for `generateContent` synchronously.\n\n\n**Optimizing AI Response**\n\nI\'m now focused on significantly improving response times. Streaming answers is a priority, so I\'m investigating Server-Sent Events (SSE) using `ai.models.generateContentStream` from the Gemini SDK. I\'m also planning an SSE route like `POST /api/tutor/chat/stream`, sending chunks as they arrive for real-time updates. Additionally, I\'ll trim the history sent to the AI, keeping only the last 6-8 turns to reduce unnecessary data transfer. Finally, I\'m considering using `gemini-3.8-flash` with a low thinking level for faster responses.\n\n\n**Addressing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now diving into quota management and error handling. I need to gracefully manage 429 and 503 errors, avoiding retry loops that exhaust quotas. Additionally, I must implement a clean loading indicator during AI generation, improving the user experience for streaming content.\n\nI\'m also working on fixing the math formatting. The existing regex parser in `FormattedContent.tsx` fails on complex LaTeX. I\'m installing and configuring KaTeX to properly render inline and block equations, including chemistry notation, fractions, and standard LaTeX syntax for enhanced display.\n\n\n**Enhancing Equation Rendering**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing KaTeX for the proper rendering of mathematical expressions. My primary concern is providing complete LaTeX support, including powers (x^2), subscripts (H_2O), square roots, Greek letters, math symbols and handling of complicated equations. I\'m also addressing Markdown formatting which includes tables, headings, bold/italic, lists, blockquotes, code blocks. It is crucial to implement safe sanitization to prevent unsafe HTML/JS execution. I\'ve also prepared graceful fallbacks to clean-up equations if parsing is an issue.\n\n**Refactoring Progress Data**\n\nI have removed all the pre-populated progress data from the system, as well as fixing issues with the front-end dashboard, which previously fell back to fake values, if the actual progress data did not exist yet. This involves changes to both `src/services/storage.ts` and `DashboardOverview.tsx`, ensuring that the student experiences a truly clean slate upon initial use. The cleanup involved removing fake minutes, completed sessions, and streak days.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_291435"
