  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Dummy Values**\n\nI\'ve been examining the hardcoded dummy distribution values on lines 46-47 of `ProgressDashboardView.tsx`. It\'s clear that `dayValues` should be derived directly from the student\'s actual recorded study minutes, not arbitrary numbers. This necessitates a change in how `dayValues` are calculated to reflect accurate progress data.\n\n\n**Refining Study Progress Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to represent study progress accurately, particularly when a student hasn\'t studied on a particular day. My thinking is to represent a day with zero study minutes as zero, not undefined, in the data. I\'m also planning the friendly empty-state message if a student hasn\'t started studying, which seems more user-friendly. I\'m taking a look at how to reset the roadmap tasks, so new users have a clean slate, especially `task-1-1` and `task-1-2`. Finally, I\'m setting up our storage keys with a versioning strategy.\n\n\n"
