  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Goal:** Fix three core issues in the existing \"Study Flow\" student study companion application:\n     1. **Improve AI Response Speed:** Stream responses progressively via SSE, trim excessive conversation history (keep last 6\342\200\2238 turns), use `gemini-3.8-flash` with `ThinkingLevel.LOW`, prevent duplicate API calls, and show a clean streaming loading indicator.\n     2. **Fix Mathematical Formatting & AI Responses:** Fix raw Markdown and LaTeX syntax (e.g. `2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}`). Install and configure KaTeX for inline (`$...$`, `\\(...\\)`) and block (`$$...$$`, `\\[...\\]`) math, physics formulas, and chemistry equations. Never expose raw LaTeX commands or delimiters inside code formatting. Handle tables, headings, and lists properly.\n     3. **Remove All Fake and Pre-Populated Progress Data:** A new student dashboard must begin at clean 0 hours, 0 completed sessions, 0 completed roadmaps, 0 assessments, 0% progress, and 0-day streak with encouraging empty states (\"No study activity yet. Start your first learning session!\", etc.). Only genuine student actions (timer completion, roadmap task toggle, quiz submission) update progress.\n   - **Target App ID:** `a8be0d2c-b06c-4918-b266-9068b9b84c8d`\n   - **Constraints:** Full-stack Express + Vite on port 3000; Gemini API calls server-side only; preserve dark navy/violet design, branding, and all 4 working features (AI Tutor, Roadmap, Paper Analyzer, Focus Tools).\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed:**\n     - `package.json`: Installed `katex` (^0.16.21) and `@types/katex`.\n     - `index.html`: Added KaTeX stylesheet link from CDN in `<head>`.\n     - `src/services/storage.ts`: Cleaned `initialRoadmap` so tasks default to `completed: false`; created `cleanInitialProgress` with all 0s and empty arrays; sanitized `getProgress()` and `getRoadmaps()` to strip legacy dummy data (`session-1`, `session-2`, `185` mins); added `resetProgress()`.\n     - `src/components/DashboardOverview.tsx`: Removed hardcoded fallback stats (`3.1 hrs`, `4 Days`, `84%`) so new students see 0 hours, 0 streak, and 0% mastery.\n     - `src/components/ProgressDashboardView.tsx`: Replaced hardcoded dummy weekly distribution with `getPast7DaysData()` from genuine `sessionLogs`; added `completedRoadmapsCount` and `handleResetData()`.\n   - **In Progress / Remaining:**\n     - `server.ts`: Add `/api/tutor/chat/stream` SSE endpoint utilizing `ai.models.generateContentStream` with `thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW }`, history trimming (last 6\342\200\2238 messages), and proper 429/503 handling without infinite retries on quota exhaustion.\n     - `src/components/FormattedContent.tsx`: Replace naive regex parser with a robust KaTeX + Markdown renderer (supporting inline `$..$`, `\\(..\\)`, block `$$..$$`, `\\[..\\]`, tables, blockquotes, chemistry arrows `\\longrightarrow`, `\\text{}`, superscripts/subscripts, fractions `\\frac{}{}`, square roots `\\sqrt{}`).\n     - `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`: Connect to `/api/tutor/chat/stream` for progressive text streaming; add streaming cursor/spinner; trim messages before sending; handle in-flight cancellation/debouncing.\n     - `src/components/ProgressDashboardView.tsx`: Finish updating the weekly chart render and empty-state displays for 0 sessions, 0 roadmaps, and 0 quizzes.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - `ThinkingLevel.LOW` is required on `gemini-3.8-flash` to minimize model reasoning latency without sacrificing explanation quality. `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL` is not supported on 3.8-flash (returns 400).\n   - In KaTeX, chemistry equations like `2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}` render with standard KaTeX when `throwOnError: false`. For edge cases where delimiters are omitted by the model, pre-replacing `\\longrightarrow` -> `\\rightarrow` or converting raw LaTeX commands before KaTeX rendering prevents unrendered LaTeX syntax from leaking.\n   - Trimming chat history to the last 6 messages (`messages.slice(-6)`) drastically reduces Gemini prompt token processing time and accelerates response generation.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - *Error:* `setErrorMsg` TypeScript error in `AITutorView.tsx` after replacing error state.\n     *Fix:* Replaced `setErrorMsg` with `setActiveError` in file upload size validation.\n   - *Error:* Upstream Gemini 503 transient spike occurred in previous turns.\n     *Fix:* Implemented exponential retry with jitter + supported model fallback (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite`).\n   - *Note:* Do not retry on 429 quota exhaustion; surface `USAGE_LIMIT_429` immediately.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Full-stack dev server runs via `tsx server.ts` on port 3000.\n   - `gemini-3.8-flash` is active with `GEMINI_API_KEY` present in environment.\n\n6. **Next Steps (Priority Order)**\n   1. **Update `server.ts`:**\n      - Add `/api/tutor/chat/stream` SSE endpoint:\n        - Set SSE headers (`Content-Type: text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `Connection: keep-alive`).\n        - Trim `messages` to the last 6 entries.\n        - Call `ai.models.generateContentStream` with `model: PRIMARY_MODEL` and `thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW }`.\n        - Stream chunks as SSE events (`data: {\"chunk\": \"...\"}`).\n        - Parse suggestions and quiz at completion and send `data: {\"done\": true, \"suggestions\": [...], \"quiz\": [...]}`.\n        - Return friendly error JSON on failure without retrying 429 quota errors.\n   2. **Rewrite `src/components/FormattedContent.tsx` with KaTeX:**\n      - Import `katex` from `\'katex\'`.\n      - Detect and render block equations (`$$...$$`, `\\[...\\]`) and inline equations (`$...$`, `\\(...\\)`) using `katex.renderToString(expr, { displayMode, throwOnError: false })`.\n      - Pre-process LaTeX to convert `\\longrightarrow` -> `\\rightarrow`, format chemical formulas `2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}` cleanly.\n      - Render Markdown tables (`| ... |`), headings, bold/italic, lists, and SVG diagrams (`xml:svg`).\n   3. **Update `src/components/AITutorView.tsx` for Progressive Streaming:**\n      - Consume `/api/tutor/chat/stream` via `fetch` + `ReadableStream` / `TextDecoder`.\n      - Incrementally append text chunks to the model response message in real-time.\n      - Show a clean streaming indicator/cursor while receiving chunks.\n   4. **Update `src/components/ProgressDashboardView.tsx` Empty States:**\n      - Ensure the weekly chart displays empty-state when total study minutes is 0: *\"No study activity yet. Start your first learning session!\"*.\n      - Ensure Roadmap section displays: *\"Your completed roadmaps will appear here.\"*.\n      - Ensure Assessment section displays: *\"Your progress will grow as you study.\"*.\n   5. **Verification & Testing:**\n      - Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n      - Test 1: Ask Newton\'s Second Law; verify progressive streaming.\n      - Test 2: Ask water formation; verify `2H\342\202\202 + O\342\202\202 \342\206\222 2H\342\202\202O` rendering with KaTeX.\n      - Test 3: Ask quadratic formula / fractions / square roots; verify math rendering.\n      - Test 4: Verify all dashboard metrics start at 0.\n      - Test 5: Complete Pomodoro session and roadmap task; verify real progress recorded and preserved across refresh.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Keep dark navy/charcoal + purple/violet SaaS aesthetic.\n   - Zero hardcoded fake progress data for new students.\n   - Do not display raw LaTeX commands (`\\text{}`, `\\longrightarrow`, `\\frac{}{}`).\n   - Preserve all 4 pillars and existing saved conversations.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 235
