    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Build : Build an modern , friendly, full stack , AI powered student study corner which they can learn new stuff , \nanalyze their progress and time themselves which will be called Study Flow\n\nTageline. Your Studies , Your Pace , Your Success \n\nStudy Flow is an all-in-one study companion that helps studens understand difficult concepts, prepare for examinations\n,organise their study schedules and manage their time.\n\nThe platform should contain four main features: \n\nAI Personal Tutor: An interactive AI tutor that explains concepts, answers follow-up questions, provides diagrams when useful and assesses students after they understand a topic.\nAI Study Roadmap: Students upload a chapter or syllabus, provide their available study time and deadline, and receive a personalised daily study plan.\nAI Paper Analyzer: Students upload examination papers, and AI identifies topics, classifies questions by difficulty (Easy, Moderate and Hard), and prioritises topics for revision.\nFocus Tools: Include a Pomodoro timer and stopwatch to help students manage their study sessions.\n\nAlso include personal progress dashboard and a notes section . The application should be fully functional , not just a visual prototype.\n\n\n\nUser: The target audience is school and college students, particularly students preparing for examinations.\n\nThe platform should support students with different academic levels, learning abilities and study schedules.\n\nStudents may struggle with:\n\n* Understanding difficult academic concepts.\n* Managing their study time.\n* Completing large chapters before deadlines.\n* Knowing which topics to prioritise.\n* Analysing examination papers.\n* Tracking their academic progress.\n\nStudy Flow should act as a helpful personal study companion.\n\nThe interface and explanations should be simple, friendly and easy to understand, even for students with limited technical knowledge.\n\n\nInterface: Create a clean dashboard with a left-hand navigation sidebar.\n\nInclude the following sections:\n\n1. Dashboard\n\n   * Welcome message.\n   * Overview of study activity.\n   * Quick access to all four main features.\n   * Study progress and recent activities.\n\n2. AI Tutor\n\n   * Conversational chat interface.\n   * Message input and send button.\n   * Formatted explanations and mathematical equations.\n   * Diagrams when useful.\n   * Saved conversations.\n   * Optional assessments.\n\n3. Study Roadmap\n\n   * Chapter and syllabus upload.\n   * Subject and deadline inputs.\n   * Daily study-time selection.\n   * AI-generated daily schedule.\n   * Interactive completion checklist.\n   * Progress indicator.\n   * Start Learning button connected to AI Tutor.\n\n4. Paper Analyzer\n\n   * PDF and image upload.\n   * Paper analysis results.\n   * Easy, Moderate and Hard classifications.\n   * High, Medium and Low topic priorities.\n   * Revision recommendations.\n\n(For Ai tuitor,Study Roadmap , Paper Analyzer Should handle large files and the result should be generate in less time)\n\n5. Focus Tools\n\n   * Pomodoro timer.\n   * Stopwatch.\n   * Start, pause and reset controls.\n   * Customisable focus and break durations.\n\n6. My Progress\n\n   * Study time statistics.\n   * Completed roadmaps.\n   * Assessment results.\n   * Learning activity.\n\n7. My Notes\n\n   * Create and save notes.\n   * Organise notes by subject.\n   * Save important formulas and explanations.\n\nEvery navigation item, button and interactive component must work properly.\n\n\n\nLooks : Use a modern, futuristic and premium educational SaaS design.\n\nVisual direction:\n\n* Dark navy and deep charcoal background.\n* Purple and electric violet accent colours.\n* Subtle gradients and soft glowing highlights.\n* Clean cards with rounded corners.\n* Modern typography.\n* Minimal and elegant icons.\n* Smooth, subtle animations.\n* Clear visual hierarchy.\n\nThe design should feel like a premium AI productivity platform rather than a traditional school website.\n\nUse a consistent design system across every section.\n\nDashboard:\n\n* Modern welcome section.\n* Elegant feature cards.\n* Study statistics.\n* Progress bars.\n* Recent activity.\n\nAI Tutor:\n\n* Clean conversational layout.\n* Readable messages.\n* Beautifully rendered formulas.\n* Visually clear diagrams.\n\nStudy Roadmap:\n\n* Attractive timeline or calendar layout.\n* Organised daily study cards.\n* Clear completion indicators.\n\nPaper Analyzer:\n\n* Professional upload area.\n* Easy-to-understand difficulty indicators.\n* Organised analysis results.\n\nFocus Tools:\n\n* Large, readable timer.\n* Minimal controls.\n* Clear focus and break indicators.\n\nEnsure the entire website is responsive and looks excellent on desktop, tablet and mobile.\n\n\nDetails: \nFUNCTIONALITY REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. AI INTEGRATION\n   Use a supported AI API for actual tutoring, roadmap generation and paper analysis. Do not use  answers as substitutes for real AI functionality.\n\n2. FILE UPLOADS\n   Support PDF and image uploads where technically possible. Handle large documents sensibly and provide clear upload and processing status.\n\n3. DATA STORAGE\n   Save study roadmaps, conversations, notes and progress. Data should remain available after refreshing the website.\n\n4. AI TUTOR\n   Maintain conversation context, explain concepts simply, support follow-up questions and offer assessments only when the student is ready.\n\n5. STUDY ROADMAP\n   Generate realistic daily schedules based on the student\'s available time and deadline. Never invent textbook contents or claim that uncompleted sessions are completed.\n\n6. PAPER ANALYZER\n   Analyse the actual uploaded paper. Explain why topics are prioritised and classify difficulty based on the questions.\n\n7. FOCUS TIMER\n   Ensure Pomodoro and stopwatch controls work accurately, including pause, resume and reset.\n\n8. USER EXPERIENCE\n   Include loading indicators, success messages, useful error messages and retry options.\n\n9. SECURITY\n   Keep API keys in secure server-side environment variables. Never expose credentials in frontend code.\n\n10. QUALITY\n    Make all four main features functional. Test the main workflows and fix errors before adding unnecessary decorative features.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nPrioritise a working application over a large number of unfinished features. Preserve data correctly and do not display fake AI results or progress."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Fix the AI Tutor\'s error handling in my existing Study Flow application.\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nWhen a student asks a question, the AI sometimes returns:\n\n503 UNAVAILABLE: This model is currently experiencing high demand.\n\nThe application displays the raw JSON error directly inside the chat.\n\nIMPLEMENT THESE IMPROVEMENTS:\n\n1. Handle temporary 503 errors properly.\n\n   * Implement automatic retries using exponential backoff.\n   * Use a maximum of 3 retry attempts.\n   * Add small random delays between retries.\n   * Avoid sending duplicate messages or creating duplicate AI responses.\n\n2. Improve the user interface.\n   Instead of displaying raw JSON, show:\n\n   \"Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment.\"\n\n   Include a clear Retry button.\n\n3. Preserve the student\'s question.\n   If a request fails, keep the original message in the chat so the student does not have to type it again.\n\n4. Handle other errors separately.\n\n   * 429: Explain that the usage limit has been reached.\n   * 401: Explain that API authentication needs attention.\n   * 503: Explain that the AI service is temporarily unavailable.\n   * Network errors: Explain that the connection failed.\n\n5. Model availability:\n   Inspect the currently configured Gemini model.\n   If it is temporarily overloaded, use a configured alternative model only if it is supported by the current API and project.\n   Do not invent model names or switch to paid services.\n\n6. Preserve all existing features, including conversational memory, diagrams, mathematical formatting, saved chats and Study Roadmap integration.\n\n7. Test the error-handling workflow using simulated 503 and 429 responses. Confirm that failed requests can be retried without duplicating messages.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not merely hide the error. Fix the underlying request-handling logic and display useful messages to students."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Improve my existing STUDY FLOW application by fixing three important problems.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nInspect the existing code before making changes. Preserve the current design, branding, layout and working features. Do not rebuild the application unnecessarily.\n\n## 1. IMPROVE AI RESPONSE SPEED\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe AI Tutor takes too long to generate answers.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\n* Investigate the actual reason for slow responses.\n* Check whether unnecessary API requests are being made.\n* Prevent duplicate API calls.\n* Avoid sending excessive conversation history with every request.\n* Preserve enough conversation context for meaningful follow-up questions.\n* Use a suitable, fast AI model supported by the current API configuration.\n* Implement streaming responses so answers appear progressively instead of waiting for the entire response.\n* Avoid unnecessary image generation when a simple SVG or CSS diagram would work.\n* Keep explanations accurate and useful. Do not sacrifice quality just to make responses shorter.\n* Show a clean loading indicator while the AI is responding.\n* Handle 429 and 503 errors properly with appropriate retry options.\n* Do not repeatedly retry requests that have exhausted their quota.\n\nThe goal is to make the AI Tutor responsive and reduce unnecessary waiting.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do not claim that all delays can be eliminated. If the AI provider is experiencing high demand, show an honest temporary-unavailability message.\n\n## 2. FIX MATHEMATICAL FORMATTING AND AI RESPONSES\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe AI currently displays raw Markdown and LaTeX syntax.\n\nFor example, it displays:\n\n2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\n\nInstead of displaying a properly formatted chemical equation.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\nA. MARKDOWN FORMATTING\n\nProperly render:\n\n* Headings.\n* Bold and italic text.\n* Bullet points.\n* Numbered lists.\n* Tables.\n* Blockquotes.\n* Code blocks when actual code is being displayed.\n\nNever expose raw Markdown formatting symbols to students when they should be rendered.\n\nB. MATHEMATICAL FORMATTING\n\nImplement a reliable mathematical rendering system such as KaTeX.\n\nSupport:\n\n* Inline equations.\n* Block equations.\n* Fractions.\n* Powers and exponents.\n* Subscripts.\n* Square roots.\n* Greek letters.\n* Mathematical symbols.\n* Chemical equations.\n* Physics formulas.\n* Units and scientific notation.\n\nUse standard mathematical delimiters:\n\n* $...$ for inline equations.\n* \\(...\\) for separate equations.\n\nDo not display mathematical expressions inside code formatting.\n\nExamples of how equations should appear:\n\nPhysics:\n\nF = m \303\227 a\n\nChemistry:\n\n2H\342\202\202 + O\342\202\202 \342\206\222 2H\342\202\202O\n\nMathematics:\n\nx = (-b \302\261 \342\210\232(b\302\262 - 4ac)) / 2a\n\nAlso explain the meaning of symbols underneath equations whenever appropriate.\n\nC. VISUAL PRESENTATION\n\n* Display equations clearly and separately from paragraphs when necessary.\n* Ensure formulas are readable on mobile and desktop.\n* Use proper spacing between explanations and equations.\n* Handle incomplete or invalid mathematical expressions gracefully.\n* Sanitize rendered AI content to prevent unsafe HTML or JavaScript execution.\n* Do not display raw LaTeX commands such as \\text{}, \\longrightarrow or \\frac{}{}.\n\nInspect the existing rendering pipeline and fix the actual problem rather than simply changing the AI prompt.\n\nDo not break the existing chat interface or conversational history.\n\n## 3. REMOVE ALL FAKE AND PRE-POPULATED PROGRESS DATA\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe website currently displays progress statistics and study activities even when a student has not actually completed them.\n\nI want STUDY FLOW to begin with a clean and honest dashboard.\n\nRemove all:\n\n* Fake completed study sessions.\n* Pre-filled study hours.\n* Artificial streaks.\n* Fake assessment scores.\n* Sample completed roadmaps.\n* Invented learning statistics.\n* Fake progress percentages.\n* Artificial recent activities.\n* Hardcoded achievements.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\nA. NEW STUDENT EXPERIENCE\n\nWhen a new student opens Study Flow, display:\n\n* Total study time: 0 hours.\n* Completed sessions: 0.\n* Completed roadmaps: 0.\n* Assessments completed: 0.\n* Learning progress: 0%.\n\nShow friendly empty-state messages such as:\n\n\"No study activity yet. Start your first learning session!\"\n\n\"Your completed roadmaps will appear here.\"\n\n\"Your progress will grow as you study.\"\n\nB. REAL PROGRESS TRACKING\n\nOnly update progress when the student actually performs an action.\n\nExamples:\n\n* A study session counts after it is genuinely completed.\n* A roadmap session counts after the student marks it completed.\n* Assessment statistics update after an assessment is submitted and checked.\n* Study time updates based on actual recorded timer sessions.\n* Streaks update based on real study activity.\n\nC. DATA STORAGE\n\n* Save genuine progress using the existing persistence system.\n* Restore saved progress after refreshing the website.\n* Do not reset existing real student data.\n* Do not overwrite real progress with sample data.\n* Keep different students\' data separate where user accounts are supported.\n\nD. SAMPLE DATA\n\nIf sample or demonstration data is necessary for development, keep it separate from real student accounts.\n\nDo not show sample data in the normal student dashboard.\n\n## 4. FINAL TESTING\n\nAfter making these changes, test:\n\nTEST 1:\nAsk the AI Tutor to explain Newton\'s Second Law. Check whether the answer appears progressively and without unnecessary delays.\n\nTEST 2:\nAsk it to explain the formation of water. Check that the chemical equation is properly formatted.\n\nTEST 3:\nAsk a question involving fractions, powers and square roots. Confirm that the mathematical formatting works.\n\nTEST 4:\nOpen a new student account or a clean dashboard state. Confirm that every progress statistic begins at zero.\n\nTEST 5:\nComplete an actual Pomodoro session and a roadmap session. Confirm that genuine progress is recorded correctly.\n\nTEST 6:\nRefresh the website and confirm that real saved progress remains available.\n\nIMPORTANT FINAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n\n* Preserve all four main features: AI Tutor, Study Roadmap, Paper Analyzer and Focus Tools.\n* Preserve existing saved conversations and genuine student data.\n* Do not replace working features with static mockups.\n* Do not introduce fake responses, fake progress or decorative buttons.\n* Make actual code changes and verify the results.\n* Prioritise reliability, speed, accuracy and a clean user experience."
    }
  }
}
