  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Response Bottlenecks**\n\nI\'m digging into the slow AI response times, focusing initially on `server.ts` and `AITutorView.tsx`. The goal is to pinpoint the specific cause, which could be anything from server-side bottlenecks to inefficiencies in the streaming implementation. I need to understand what\'s actually slowing things down before making any changes.\n\n\n**Optimizing Streaming Implementation**\n\nI\'ve trimmed the chat history to the last six messages to reduce data transfer. Implementing an SSE stream endpoint, `/api/tutor/chat/stream`, will provide immediate feedback. On `gemini-3.8-flash`, I\'m setting `thinkingConfig` to low. Duplicate API calls are being addressed with debouncing, or an abort controller, to avoid sending multiple requests while loading. Finally, I\'m working on robust error handling for 429 and 503 errors.\n\n\n**Testing Error Handling Robustness**\n\nI\'m now focusing on error simulation within the AI interaction. I\'m injecting various error scenarios, such as 503, 429, 401 and network errors, to test the robustness of the system\'s error handling. I\'m ensuring all expected error codes are correctly caught and handled, to make the system more resilient. The simulated errors currently include a variety of error responses to ensure there are no single points of failure.\n\n\n**Defining Tutor Characteristics**\n\nMy current focus is on defining the core characteristics of this personal tutor. I want to ensure it\342\200\231s warm, inspiring, and adaptable. I\'m prioritizing clear, step-by-step explanations, breaking down complex topics into intuitive components. The objective is to make advanced concepts accessible through relatable analogies and examples. I must also correctly format scientific notation, equations, and chemical reactions.\n\n\n**Refining Tutor Response Style**\n\nI am now fine-tuning the tutor\'s response style. I need to make sure the tutor handles mathematical and chemical equations correctly, never displaying them as raw text in code blocks. I must also add visual aids such as SVG diagrams where they enhance understanding, especially for geometric figures, biology processes, and chemical cycles. Finally, I will ensure follow-up questions and assessments are appropriately provided at the end.\n\n\n**Implementing Quiz Functionality**\n\nI\'m working on generating quizzes automatically. I\'m focusing on crafting a structured quiz format that includes questions, answer options, correct answer indices, and explanations for each question. I\'ll trigger the quiz after a topic has been fully explained, or when a student requests it. The questions will be concise, focusing on core concepts.\n\n\n**Enhancing Lesson Prompting**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on refining the initial lesson prompt to improve learning outcomes. I\'m adding a prompt that focuses the tutor to respond with an initial \"Hello Tutor!\" message. Additionally, I\'m integrating logic to guide responses based on the provided topic and learner requests. I\'m integrating quiz requests at the end of lessons, when requested.\n\n\n**Parsing Response Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on parsing the full text response to extract specific elements. I\'m extracting and handling suggestions and quiz data using regular expressions and JSON parsing. The current strategy is to find blocks denoted by `<<<SUGGESTIONS: ... >>>` and `<<<QUIZ: ... >>>`. I\'m using `JSON.parse` to extract the relevant data and handling potential parsing errors.\n\n\n**Refactoring Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve refactored the error handling in `/api/tutor/chat/stream`, adding logic to respond with appropriate JSON formats when errors occur during stream processing. I\'m ensuring both the SSE stream and the regular `/api/tutor/chat` endpoint accurately reflect error details. The existing `/api/tutor/chat` endpoint is being optimized with history trimming, lower thinking level, and enhanced instructions. I\'m addressing Markdown formatting issues in `FormattedContent.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Math Rendering**\n\nI\'m now integrating KaTeX to accurately render mathematical expressions. I\'m focusing on parsing and displaying inline equations using `$...$` and block equations with `$$...$$` delimiters. I must ensure correct rendering of fractions, powers, subscripts, square roots, Greek letters, and common mathematical symbols, as well as chemical and physics formulas, and units with scientific notation.\n\n\n**Integrating KaTeX Rendering**\n\nI\'m now fully focusing on KaTeX integration for accurate equation rendering, especially chemistry notation. I\'ve confirmed that KaTeX gracefully handles various LaTeX constructs like `\\text{}`, subscripts, fractions, and arrows. I\'m focusing on parsing and rendering chemical equations properly, and improving `FormattedContent.tsx` to handle both delimited and standalone LaTeX. I will also make sure to render any other equations and formulas.\n\n\n**Enhancing Content Rendering**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust content detection within `FormattedContent.tsx` to handle various formats. I\'m focusing on parsing Markdown tables, using pipes and a header separator for HTML table rendering. I\'m also working on detecting block equations, both multi- and single-line, and even those with pure LaTeX. Finally, code blocks using ``` are getting a special parsing case so that math and latex code is rendered with KaTeX. I\'m also improving inline equation parsing.\n\n\n**Implementing KaTeX Rendering**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `renderKatex` helper to safely render LaTeX expressions within React. I\'m focusing on handling both inline and block equations, ensuring proper HTML and MathML output. I\'m rigorously testing the physics and chemistry formulas, such as $F = m \\times a$ and $2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$, to confirm correct rendering.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Empty States**\n\nI\'m now implementing empty states and ensuring a clean start for new student dashboards. Specifically, I\'m focusing on zeroing out progress metrics such as study time, completed sessions, and streak. Empty states will appear in the dashboard, with encouraging messages. The weekly chart shows a \"No study activity yet\" message. I\'ll make sure only actual student actions, like completed sessions, are counted.\n\n\n"
