  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Streaming APIs**\n\nI\'m currently investigating how `sendMessage` and `handleRetry` can work together, leveraging `/api/tutor/chat/stream` for efficient SSE streaming with `fetch`. I\'m focused on the implementation details using a POST method, including appropriate headers and request bodies. My immediate aim is to understand the complete interaction flow.\n\n\n**Analyzing Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve been examining the error handling strategy within the streaming context, particularly focusing on how to manage non-OK responses from the server. My process involves parsing JSON error data from the response, extracting friendly error messages and codes, and setting an `activeError` state that includes the relevant details like the failed message ID and pending content. Conversely, for successful responses, I\'m defining a model placeholder message with a unique ID and initializing variables to capture streamed content, suggestions and quiz, before establishing a readable stream.\n\n\n**Refining Chunk Processing**\n\nI\'m now refining the chunk processing logic within the SSE stream. My focus is on robustly handling individual data lines. I am concentrating on the proper decoding of incoming chunks, error detection within the streamed data, and updating the UI with content. I\'m prioritizing the efficient splitting of the buffer to extract JSON strings and then selectively processing data based on the presence of chunk data or errors, all while updating messages as they come in.\n\n\n**Finalizing Content Handling**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing how the content from the stream is handled after parsing. I\'m focusing on text cleaning and structuring the data before saving. I am removing irrelevant suggestions and quiz markups, creating a final chat message, and updating the state with it. Ultimately, I am saving the updated session data to persist the entire conversation for the user, and I am clearing any active errors that might have occurred.\n\n\n**Confirming UI Streaming**\n\nI\'m verifying the UI rendering during streaming, specifically in the `handleRetry` function, ensuring the same streaming mechanism is used with `updatedSessionMessages` to preserve the student\'s original question. I\'ve confirmed that `currentFullText` updates dynamically via `FormattedContent`, showing progressive content to the student. During the `loading` state, I\'m working to show an appropriate indicator, displaying \"AI Tutor is preparing your explanation...\" when content is empty and a pulsing cursor or active streaming indicator when content is present.\n\n\n"
