    thinking: "**Analyzing System Response**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the response from task-317. It looks like the AI tutor is temporarily unavailable, returning a 503 error, model busy. This confirms a system-level issue and I am now considering alternative methods to circumvent the issue.\n\n\n**Evaluating Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve confirmed our 503 error handling is working correctly. The server intercepts the model busy error, presents a user-friendly message, and preserves the original question. I\'m also investigating if `FALLBACK_MODEL` (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite`) can be retried when the primary model is unavailable.\n\n\n**Investigating Network Response**\n\nI\'ve just revisited the 503 error scenario related to task-317. It seems the issue stemmed from both primary and fallback models being unavailable, throwing a `streamInitErr`. The error handling in `server.ts` correctly returned a JSON response reflecting this temporary unavailability, including the status code, error code and a user friendly message as specified. I am now looking at improving the retry logic.\n\n\n**Refining Client-Side Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the client-side display for handling non-OK responses from the AI tutor. Instead of raw JSON, I\'ll be presenting a more user-friendly message: \"Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment.\" It will also include a clear Retry button, ensuring the student\'s question is preserved. I\'ve confirmed `AITutorView.tsx` correctly handles non-OK statuses, removing the placeholder and keeping the user\'s input.\n\n\n"
