  planner_response {
    response: "I have resolved all three issues across the **Study Flow** application:\n\n### 1. AI Response Speed & Progressive Streaming\n* **Server-Sent Events (SSE) Streaming:** Implemented `/api/tutor/chat/stream` using `@google/genai` `ai.models.generateContentStream`, rendering responses incrementally in real time so students no longer wait for the entire response to generate.\n* **Low-Latency Thinking Configuration:** Configured `thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW }` on `gemini-3.8-flash` to minimize model reasoning latency while maintaining high pedagogical depth.\n* **Context Trimming:** Truncated conversation payload to the last 6 messages (`messages.slice(-6)`), eliminating excessive prompt token overhead and duplicate requests.\n* **Fallback & Transient Error Handling:** Added exponential backoff and automatic failover to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` on transient 503 high-demand spikes, with immediate surfacing of 429 quota exhaustion notices without wasteful loops.\n* **Preserved Questions & Retry:** If upstream AI spikes occur, questions remain preserved in the chat with a clear *\"Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment\"* card and a one-click **Retry Question** action.\n\n### 2. Mathematical & Chemical Formatting with KaTeX\n* **KaTeX Rendering Engine:** Integrated KaTeX for inline equations (`$...$`, `\\(...\\)`) and block equations (`$$...$$`, `\\[...\\]`).\n* **Chemistry & Physics Support:** Chemical reactions (such as $$2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$$), physics formulas ($F = m \\times a$, $E = mc^2$), fractions ($\\frac{a}{b}$), and roots ($\\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}$) are now rendered with typography and symbol explanations instead of raw code blocks.\n* **Full Markdown & Diagram Support:** Rendered markdown tables (`|...|`), headings, blockquotes, and interactive SVG concept diagrams with expand and copy tools.\n\n### 3. Clean Zero-State Progress & Genuine Tracking\n* **Zero Dummy Data:** Removed all hardcoded fallback stats (e.g. 3.1 hrs, 4-day streak, 84% score). New students start at 0 hours, 0 completed roadmaps, 0 quizzes, and 0-day streaks.\n* **Encouraging Empty States:** Added helpful empty states:\n  * *\"No study activity yet. Start your first learning session!\"* with a direct focus timer launcher.\n  * *\"Your completed roadmaps will appear here.\"*\n  * *\"Your progress will grow as you study.\"*\n* **Real Metric Logging:** Total study time, weekly distribution charts, streaks, and mastery scores only increment through genuine student activity (Pomodoro/stopwatch timer completions, roadmap task toggles, and assessment quiz submissions)."
    thinking: "**Verifying Progress**\n\nI\'m thrilled to report that both `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` are error-free! Now, I\'m meticulously re-examining the user prompt, along with the truncated compaction summary, to ensure complete accuracy. Specifically, I\'m focusing on refining the AI response speed and optimizing token usage. I\'ve trimmed the history to the last six messages, significantly reducing the prompt\'s size.\n\n\n**Optimizing AI Interactions**\n\nI\'ve been working on improving the user experience during AI interactions. I\'ve switched to `gemini-3.8-flash` with a low `thinkingLevel`, and implemented an SSE streaming endpoint for more progressive responses. Debouncing the send button and loading indicators are also in place. Furthermore, I\'ve integrated KaTeX for beautiful mathematical formatting with support for a broad range of LaTeX elements. Finally, I\'ve cleared all the prepopulated progress.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have resolved all three issues across the **Study Flow** application:\n\n### 1. AI Response Speed & Progressive Streaming\n* **Server-Sent Events (SSE) Streaming:** Implemented `/api/tutor/chat/stream` using `@google/genai` `ai.models.generateContentStream`, rendering responses incrementally in real time so students no longer wait for the entire response to generate.\n* **Low-Latency Thinking Configuration:** Configured `thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW }` on `gemini-3.8-flash` to minimize model reasoning latency while maintaining high pedagogical depth.\n* **Context Trimming:** Truncated conversation payload to the last 6 messages (`messages.slice(-6)`), eliminating excessive prompt token overhead and duplicate requests.\n* **Fallback & Transient Error Handling:** Added exponential backoff and automatic failover to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` on transient 503 high-demand spikes, with immediate surfacing of 429 quota exhaustion notices without wasteful loops.\n* **Preserved Questions & Retry:** If upstream AI spikes occur, questions remain preserved in the chat with a clear *\"Our AI tutor is temporarily busy. Please try again in a moment\"* card and a one-click **Retry Question** action.\n\n### 2. Mathematical & Chemical Formatting with KaTeX\n* **KaTeX Rendering Engine:** Integrated KaTeX for inline equations (`$...$`, `\\(...\\)`) and block equations (`$$...$$`, `\\[...\\]`).\n* **Chemistry & Physics Support:** Chemical reactions (such as $$2\\text{H}_2 + \\text{O}_2 \\longrightarrow 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$$), physics formulas ($F = m \\times a$, $E = mc^2$), fractions ($\\frac{a}{b}$), and roots ($\\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}$) are now rendered with typography and symbol explanations instead of raw code blocks.\n* **Full Markdown & Diagram Support:** Rendered markdown tables (`|...|`), headings, blockquotes, and interactive SVG concept diagrams with expand and copy tools.\n\n### 3. Clean Zero-State Progress & Genuine Tracking\n* **Zero Dummy Data:** Removed all hardcoded fallback stats (e.g. 3.1 hrs, 4-day streak, 84% score). New students start at 0 hours, 0 completed roadmaps, 0 quizzes, and 0-day streaks.\n* **Encouraging Empty States:** Added helpful empty states:\n  * *\"No study activity yet. Start your first learning session!\"* with a direct focus timer launcher.\n  * *\"Your completed roadmaps will appear here.\"*\n  * *\"Your progress will grow as you study.\"*\n* **Real Metric Logging:** Total study time, weekly distribution charts, streaks, and mastery scores only increment through genuine student activity (Pomodoro/stopwatch timer completions, roadmap task toggles, and assessment quiz submissions)."
