  user_input {
    user_response: "Fix the AI Tutor chat interface layout in my existing Study Flow website.\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\nThe message input box where students type their questions is appearing at the top of the chat interface.\n\nEXPECTED BEHAVIOUR:\n\n1. Move the message input box to the bottom of the AI Tutor chat area.\n2. Keep it visible while the student scrolls through previous messages.\n3. Display conversation messages above the input box.\n4. Make the message history independently scrollable.\n5. Automatically scroll to the latest message when a new message arrives, without forcing the student to scroll when they are reading older messages.\n6. Keep the input box accessible while the AI is generating a response.\n7. Support multiline text input.\n8. Keep the Send button beside the input box.\n9. Make the layout responsive on mobile, tablet and desktop.\n10. Ensure the input box never covers the last conversation message.\n\nUse a proper flex-column chat layout:\n\n* Conversation history: flexible, scrollable area.\n* Message composer: positioned at the bottom of the chat panel.\n\nPreserve the existing colours, styling, animations, AI functionality and saved conversations.\n\nDo not redesign the entire AI Tutor. Only fix the layout and positioning."
    items {
      text: "Fix the AI Tutor chat interface layout in my existing Study Flow website.\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\nThe message input box where students type their questions is appearing at the top of the chat interface.\n\nEXPECTED BEHAVIOUR:\n\n1. Move the message input box to the bottom of the AI Tutor chat area.\n2. Keep it visible while the student scrolls through previous messages.\n3. Display conversation messages above the input box.\n4. Make the message history independently scrollable.\n5. Automatically scroll to the latest message when a new message arrives, without forcing the student to scroll when they are reading older messages.\n6. Keep the input box accessible while the AI is generating a response.\n7. Support multiline text input.\n8. Keep the Send button beside the input box.\n9. Make the layout responsive on mobile, tablet and desktop.\n10. Ensure the input box never covers the last conversation message.\n\nUse a proper flex-column chat layout:\n\n* Conversation history: flexible, scrollable area.\n* Message composer: positioned at the bottom of the chat panel.\n\nPreserve the existing colours, styling, animations, AI functionality and saved conversations.\n\nDo not redesign the entire AI Tutor. Only fix the layout and positioning."
    }
  }
}
