  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App Layout**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `App.tsx` file closely. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the main container\'s styling, particularly how the `currentSection` state affects its padding and overall layout. The goal is to understand how these styles contribute to the app\'s responsive design and overall structure. I\'m noting the use of flexbox and min-height properties.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction of the `currentSection` state with specific layout attributes within the `App.tsx` file. I\'m noting that the conditional application of `h-screen`, `max-h-screen`, and `overflow-hidden` when `currentSection` is \'tutor\' creates a critical distinction. It seems to isolate the chat area from the outer browser window\'s scrolling, leading to a much better UX. Furthermore, it appears that the message composer is 100% locked to the bottom of the chat panel on all screens. This layout strategy appears to be key.\n\n\n"
