  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Interface Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of `AITutorView.tsx`, specifically focusing on the chat interface\'s structure. Lines 686-687 reveal a main div, using flexbox for layout, with styling for rounded corners, background, border, blur, and shadow. I\'m noting the use of flex-col to arrange children vertically and the overflow-hidden property. I am analyzing the code for component nesting and layout strategy.\n\n\n**Refining the Layout Logic**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `flex-1 flex flex-col` container. I\'m now certain that the missing `min-h-0` is a critical oversight. Without it, flex children within flex containers won\'t shrink properly. I\'ve also identified that the `Messages Stream` and the error banner, lines 900-979, also need `min-h-0` for correct behavior. I\'m considering alternatives to placing the error messages within the scrollable messages area, as this placement can lead to these messages being obscured from the user.\n\n\n**Addressing the UI Behavior**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI behavior related to the input field and auto-scrolling. The missing `min-h-0` on the main container and messages stream created viewport scrolling issues and input field behavior problems. The input, initially an `<input type=\"text\">`, was disabled during loading. The current auto-scroll implementation, using `scrollIntoView`, isn\'t ideal; I\'m implementing smart scrolling, tracking the student\'s scroll position to avoid unwanted jumps when reading older messages, using a `messagesContainerRef`.\n\n\n**Refining Scrolling Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the auto-scroll behavior. I need to make sure the chat scrolls to the newest messages, unless the user manually scrolls up. I\'m thinking I\'ll track whether the user has scrolled and only auto-scroll if the user hasn\'t. If the user scrolls up, a new message indicator will be shown. I\'m making sure to address the requirements for the input field placement.\n\n\n**Implementing Auto-Scrolling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the auto-scroll behavior, focusing on the message container\'s scrolling logic and ensuring the input box remains accessible during AI response generation. I\'m verifying the message container has `overflow-y-auto` and `min-h-0`. I\'m checking if the user is near the bottom (within 80px) before auto-scrolling on stream updates. If the user scrolls up, I will not force them down, and will use an indicator. The text area is not `disabled={loading}` and the send button remains beside it, for multiline text input using a text area. I\'ve considered that the layout must be responsive on mobile, tablet and desktop.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the layout for mobile and tablet devices, particularly around the chat interface. I\'m verifying the responsive padding using `p-2 sm:p-3.5` provides a clean appearance on different screen sizes. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of a mobile toggle for the sessions drawer or a clean drawer button to maximize available chat space. I\'m also addressing the positioning of the input box relative to the last message and designing it so the input box does not clip the last conversation message, by using a standard flexbox column with `shrink-0` on the composer, ending the scrollable area and the composer border.\n\n\n**Refining Input Field Behavior**\n\nI\'m now implementing the input field behavior, specifically the auto-resizing text area. I\'m focusing on resetting the textarea height after sending a message to \'auto\' to ensure it shrinks back. I\'m checking that the enter key triggers the `sendMessage` function, but prevents the default behavior. I am also checking the implementation of auto-scroll for user control.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m checking that `setInputMessage(\'\')` is called and the height of the text area is reset to auto after each message, ensuring the interface remains clean. I\'m also now analyzing the auto-scroll implementation, focusing on the `messagesContainerRef` and `shouldAutoScrollRef` to ensure messages are scrolled to the bottom only when the user is near the bottom. I am also implementing a `showScrollBottomBtn` and making sure it functions correctly, including the `scrollToBottom` function.\n\n\n"
