  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`. I\'ve added a ref, `messagesContainerRef`, to the scrollable messages div, for future manipulation. The goal here is to make this component more dynamic. I\'ll need to figure out where to place the `textarea` next.\n\n\n**Implementing Scrolling Mechanics**\n\nI\'ve integrated refs (`messagesContainerRef`, `shouldAutoScrollRef`) and state (`showScrollBottomBtn`, `mobileSidebarOpen`) to manage scrolling behavior. My recent work has centered on the `handleMessagesScroll` function, which now accurately detects when the student is near the bottom, thus enabling or disabling auto-scroll and showing the scroll-to-bottom button. I also implemented `useEffect` to ensure smooth auto-scrolling on message updates, and forced auto-scrolling when a student submits a message.\n\n\n**Refining User Interface**\n\nI\'ve just added a \"Jump to bottom\" button that appears when the user scrolls up. This button uses `messagesEndRef` to smoothly scroll the messages to the bottom. I\'ve also implemented `setShowScrollBottomBtn(false)` after jumping, and now need to import `ArrowDown` from \'lucide-react\'. Next, I\'ll be working on replacing the single-line input with a multiline textarea.\n\n\n**Evaluating Input Field Behavior**\n\nI\'ve just added a new multiline text area that allows for input even during AI response generation. I made sure that there is no `disabled={loading}`. I also confirmed that Shift+Enter creates a new line and Enter sends the message. The Send button remains beside the input field as a requirement.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mobile responsiveness for the layout, specifically ensuring the input box doesn\'t obscure the latest message. The goal is a consistently viewable conversation. The next step involves adjusting the `div` structure and applying appropriate styling to the scrollable messages area. I\'ll need to use the provided class structure to fit the content responsively.\n\n\n"
