attribute for clarity. I\'m focusing on the effect of button\'s classes and event interactions in this part of `AITutorView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Examining Key Functionality**\n\nI\'m now investigating the multiline handler, specifically how it manages the text area\'s height dynamically based on content and using Shift+Enter functionality for new lines. I\'m scrutinizing `handleTextareaChange` and `handleKeyDown` to understand the logic for adjusting height and sending messages. I\'m also examining how the input field is cleared after a message is sent within the `sendMessage` function, which resets its height. I am also checking the mobile drawer implementation.\n\n\n**Reviewing Requirements Implementation**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the user requirements one by one, to ensure all are met. I\'m confirming that the message input is fixed at the bottom, and never scrolls. I am verifying that the conversation messages are displayed above the input box in a scrollable area. I\'m also now analyzing the implementation of the sessions button. I\'m focusing on the rendering logic for the mobile drawer overlay when `mobileSessionsOpen` is true, and the desktop sidebar behavior.\n\n\n"
