    thinking: "**Adding UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on modifying `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`. My primary task is incorporating a visual element. I\'ve begun by importing `ArrowDown`. Next, I\'m adding state to control a UI button, specifically `showScrollBottomBtn`, using `useState`. This will manage the visibility of the scroll-to-bottom button.\n\n\n**Implementing Scroll Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added several refs, including `messagesContainerRef`, `textareaRef`, and `shouldAutoScrollRef`, essential for managing scroll behavior. I\'ve set up `handleMessagesScroll` to detect proximity to the bottom, and control the scroll-to-bottom button\'s visibility.  The `scrollToBottom` function facilitates both smooth and immediate scrolling, ensuring the latest content is always in view. The useEffect hook now automatically scrolls to the bottom on new messages.\n\n\n**Refining Textarea Behavior**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the text area\'s behavior, specifically handling its height dynamically. I\'ve implemented logic to adjust the height based on content, capping it at 140px. The Enter key now submits messages, except when Shift is held. In `sendMessage` and `handleRetry`, I reset the textarea height and trigger auto-scroll. The return component has a new outer container to improve behavior.\n\n\n"
