  planner_response {
    response: "The AI Tutor chat layout has been restructured using a dedicated flex-column chat architecture:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Bottom-Positioned Message Composer:**\n   * Moved the message composer to the bottom of the chat panel as a fixed flex sibling (`shrink-0 border-t border-purple-500/20 bg-slate-950/95`).\n   * The input box stays visible at all times and never covers conversation messages.\n\n2. **Independently Scrollable Message History:**\n   * Configured the conversation history area with `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`.\n   * Scrolling through older messages occurs independently within the chat history without shifting the input bar or causing page-level jumps.\n\n3. **Smart Auto-Scroll with Reading Protection:**\n   * Auto-scroll now checks whether the student is near the bottom. If the student has scrolled up to inspect previous formulas, derivations, or diagrams, incoming streaming chunks will not yank their view downward.\n   * Sending a new message automatically scrolls down to the latest message.\n   * Added a floating **Jump to latest \342\206\223** action button when scrolled up.\n\n4. **Multiline Input & AI Accessibility:**\n   * Upgraded single-line input to an auto-expanding multiline `<textarea>` with `Shift + Enter` for new lines and `Enter` to send.\n   * The text input remains fully accessible and writable while the AI is generating, allowing students to type their next question or edit notes without waiting.\n   * Aligned the **Send** button directly beside the multiline input area.\n\n5. **Responsive Mobile & Desktop Support:**\n   * Desktop displays the saved sessions drawer side-by-side (`w-64`), while mobile and tablet include a dedicated session drawer toggle button in the chat header."
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve examined the user\'s requirements thoroughly. Currently, I\'m focusing on the directive to position the message input box. I\'ve specifically targeted the composer footer, ensuring its placement at the bottom of the chat area, by utilizing the designated attributes.\n\n\n**Refining Composer Behavior**\n\nI\'m now refining the composer\'s behavior during message display. Specifically, the message composer is set as a sibling flex item that does not scroll with message history. I\'ve confirmed the message stream occupies the area directly above it, utilizing `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`. I\'m now testing the independent scrollability of the message history by using `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto custom-scrollbar`. Also, I\'m integrating automatic scrolling to the latest message using `shouldAutoScrollRef`, including a floating \"Jump to latest \342\206\223\" button. I want to keep the input box accessible while the AI is generating a response.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The AI Tutor chat layout has been restructured using a dedicated flex-column chat architecture:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Bottom-Positioned Message Composer:**\n   * Moved the message composer to the bottom of the chat panel as a fixed flex sibling (`shrink-0 border-t border-purple-500/20 bg-slate-950/95`).\n   * The input box stays visible at all times and never covers conversation messages.\n\n2. **Independently Scrollable Message History:**\n   * Configured the conversation history area with `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`.\n   * Scrolling through older messages occurs independently within the chat history without shifting the input bar or causing page-level jumps.\n\n3. **Smart Auto-Scroll with Reading Protection:**\n   * Auto-scroll now checks whether the student is near the bottom. If the student has scrolled up to inspect previous formulas, derivations, or diagrams, incoming streaming chunks will not yank their view downward.\n   * Sending a new message automatically scrolls down to the latest message.\n   * Added a floating **Jump to latest \342\206\223** action button when scrolled up.\n\n4. **Multiline Input & AI Accessibility:**\n   * Upgraded single-line input to an auto-expanding multiline `<textarea>` with `Shift + Enter` for new lines and `Enter` to send.\n   * The text input remains fully accessible and writable while the AI is generating, allowing students to type their next question or edit notes without waiting.\n   * Aligned the **Send** button directly beside the multiline input area.\n\n5. **Responsive Mobile & Desktop Support:**\n   * Desktop displays the saved sessions drawer side-by-side (`w-64`), while mobile and tablet include a dedicated session drawer toggle button in the chat header."
