  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Optimizing Response Speed**\n\nI\'m focused on improving the AI tutor\'s response speed. I\'m investigating the AI request workflow to find bottlenecks. Specifically, I\'m looking at preventing duplicate API requests by exploring debouncing or disabling the send button during request handling to prevent double triggers.\n\n\n**Analyzing Request Flow**\n\nI\'m now digging into `AITutorView.tsx`, specifically the `sendMessage` function and its associated checks. I noticed how the Enter key and Send button are disabled during loading, which is good. I\'m now shifting to the server-side, scrutinizing the `/api/tutor/chat/stream` endpoint in `server.ts`. I want to see if the system instruction or history construction might be slowing down initial token generation, and the configured `thinkingLevel`. I\'ll also confirm the fallback model and verify available options in the SDK.\n\n\n**Evaluating Model Performance**\n\nI\'m now comparing the performance of `gemini-3.8-flash` against `gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, focusing on Time To First Token (TTFT). I also need to verify the exact system prompt sent and identify fast, supported models. Furthermore, I\'ll ensure lightweight visuals are used and optimize SSE streaming for smooth, jitter-free chunking and implement proper handling of 429 and 503 errors with retries.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Note Management**\n\nI\'m now implementing note management within the system. I\'m focusing on enabling edit and delete functionality for existing notes, complete with confirmation dialogs for deletion. The changes are saved automatically, and notes will be displayed in an organized list with relevant metadata. I\'m leveraging the existing persistent storage system to ensure notes are accessible after refreshing. I\'ve located relevant files in `src/components/NotesView.tsx` and `src/services/storage.ts`. I also need to make sure we prevent accidental overwrites!\n\n**Adding Roadmap Deletion**\n\nI\'m now focused on adding a deletion feature to the study roadmap functionality. Students can create roadmaps, but they can\'t delete them. I\'m adding a three-dot menu or delete icon to each roadmap to provide a \"Delete Roadmap\" option. A confirmation dialog will appear before deletion to prevent accidental loss. I will now add this delete option.\n\n\n"
