  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - User Request: Implement three specific enhancements in Study Flow without rebuilding or breaking existing working features, styling, or saved data:\n     1. **Improve AI Tutor Response Speed**: Optimize AI request workflow, prevent duplicate requests, trim excessive conversation history while retaining context, use an appropriately fast model (`gemini-2.5-flash` or fast fallback) with low latency, stream responses, lightweight SVG/CSS diagrams, clean loading indicators, robust 429/503 handling with Retry button and preserved original question.\n     2. **Add a \"+ Create New Note\" option**: Prominent button in My Notes section opening a dedicated note editor (title, subject/category, text area, Save, Cancel), support multiple notes, editing, deletion with confirmation dialog, auto-save where appropriate, organized list showing title/subject/date, persistent storage via `StorageService` without ever overwriting existing notes.\n     3. **Add a Delete Option to Study Roadmap**: Visible 3-dot menu or delete icon on each saved roadmap, confirmation modal (\"Are you sure you want to delete this study roadmap? This action cannot be undone.\" with Cancel and Delete Roadmap buttons), remove associated schedule and completion data from persistent storage, immediate list update, recalculate progress from remaining data, navigate away if currently viewing deleted roadmap, preserve all other roadmaps/chats/notes, clean empty state when 0 roadmaps exist: \"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\".\n     4. **Test Everything**: Verify AI tutor prompt + context + error handling, Notes create + edit + delete + persist, and Roadmap create + delete + persist.\n   - Development URL: `https://ais-dev-zwqhtii5o2wun226ti5rss-476841582553.europe-west2.run.app`\n   - Shared App URL: `https://ais-pre-zwqhtii5o2wun226ti5rss-476841582553.europe-west2.run.app`\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in earlier turns**:\n     - Chat layout rewritten to a true flex-column layout with fixed bottom multiline composer, independent messages scrolling, reading-position-aware auto-scrolling, and floating \"Jump to latest\" button in `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`.\n     - Layout container locked in `src/App.tsx` (`h-screen max-h-screen overflow-hidden` for tutor section) preventing outer page double-scrollbars.\n     - SSE streaming endpoint implemented in `/server.ts` (`/api/tutor/chat/stream`) with KaTeX support in `FormattedContent.tsx`.\n     - Initial zero-state progress logic verified.\n     - Build and linting passed (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet`).\n   - **Inspected for current request**:\n     - `src/services/storage.ts`: Read lines 1-150. Contains `ROADMAPS_KEY = \'studyflow_roadmaps\'`, `NOTES_KEY = \'studyflow_notes\'`, `initialRoadmap`, `initialSampleNotes`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **AI Speed**:\n     - Currently in `server.ts`: Uses `gemini-3.8-flash` with fallback to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`. `gemini-2.5-flash` or optimized system instructions without heavy repetitive prompt engineering yields faster TTFT (Time To First Token).\n     - Streaming is already hooked up in `server.ts` and `AITutorView.tsx`. Ensure request debouncing and that the Send button and input prevent accidental rapid double-submissions.\n   - **My Notes**:\n     - `NotesView.tsx` needs a prominent `+ Create New Note` button.\n     - Note editor modal/inline view needs: `title`, `subject`/category, `content` textarea, `Save`, and `Cancel`.\n     - Note deletion needs a confirmation dialog.\n     - `StorageService` methods: need `saveNote`, `deleteNote`, `getNotes`. Must ensure new notes get unique IDs (`note-${Date.now()}`) so they never overwrite existing notes.\n   - **Study Roadmap**:\n     - `StudyRoadmapView.tsx` needs a 3-dot dropdown or delete trash icon per roadmap card/tab.\n     - Modal confirmation required with text: `\"Are you sure you want to delete this study roadmap? This action cannot be undone.\"` and buttons `Cancel` and `Delete Roadmap`.\n     - `StorageService.deleteRoadmap(id)` must remove it from localStorage and recalculate progress data (or `UserProgressData.completedRoadmaps`).\n     - Empty state required if roadmaps array is empty: `\"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\"`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - *Error*: In previous turn, upstream Gemini API returned 503 during high demand.\n     *Fix*: `server.ts` catch block handles 503 and returns structured JSON; `AITutorView.tsx` catches non-200 responses, preserves the student\'s question, displays friendly error banner with `Retry Question` button.\n   - *Error*: Long curl test command in background previously timed out waiting for stream.\n     *Fix*: Cancelled task-313; verified server health at `GET /api/health` returning 200 OK.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Express backend + Vite dev server running on port 3000.\n   - App files:\n     - `server.ts`: Express backend with Gemini streaming and API endpoints.\n     - `src/services/storage.ts`: LocalStorage management for roadmaps, notes, chats, progress.\n     - `src/components/NotesView.tsx`: Notes listing, note editing, formula sheets.\n     - `src/components/StudyRoadmapView.tsx`: Roadmap generation, day/task tracking, active roadmap view.\n     - `src/components/AITutorView.tsx`: Chat streaming, error retry, preserved questions.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Inspect `src/services/storage.ts`** (lines 150-409):\n      - Check existing roadmap and note methods (`getNotes`, `saveNote`, `deleteNote`, `getRoadmaps`, `saveRoadmap`, `deleteRoadmap`, `updateProgress`).\n      - Add `deleteRoadmap(id: string)` if missing or ensure it removes roadmap and cleans up completed roadmaps in progress data.\n   2. **Inspect & Update `src/components/NotesView.tsx`**:\n      - Add prominent `+ Create New Note` button in header.\n      - Add note creation/editing modal/form with Title, Subject/Category dropdown or text input, Content textarea, Save, and Cancel.\n      - Ensure creating a new note assigns a new unique ID (`note-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 5)}`) so it never overwrites existing notes.\n      - Add delete note confirmation dialog.\n      - Ensure notes list displays title, subject, last-updated date, and tag pills.\n   3. **Inspect & Update `src/components/StudyRoadmapView.tsx`**:\n      - Add 3-dot menu or delete icon to each roadmap item in the roadmap selector/cards.\n      - Add deletion confirmation modal with required text: `\"Are you sure you want to delete this study roadmap? This action cannot be undone.\"` and buttons `Cancel` and `Delete Roadmap`.\n      - On confirm: delete via `StorageService.deleteRoadmap(id)`, update state immediately, switch active roadmap if current was deleted, recalculate progress.\n      - Add clean empty state when no roadmaps exist: `\"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\"`.\n   4. **Audit `server.ts` & `AITutorView.tsx` for AI Speed & Stability**:\n      - Verify model configuration (`gemini-2.5-flash` or fast flash config with low latency, trimmed context).\n      - Ensure lightweight SVG/CSS diagrams instead of heavy external image calls.\n      - Ensure no duplicate requests are triggered when pressing enter or clicking send.\n   5. **Compile & Lint Verification**:\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to confirm zero TypeScript or build errors.\n      - Run functional tests using `run_command` (e.g. curl endpoints or node test scripts).\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Preserve existing branding, styles (purple/slate theme), and working features.\n   - Do NOT introduce fake notes, fake roadmaps, or artificial progress.\n   - All newly added buttons must be fully functional.\n   - Persistent storage must use `StorageService` (localStorage).\n</summary>"
