      text: "Improve my existing STUDY FLOW website by implementing the following three improvements.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nInspect the existing code before making changes. Preserve the current design, branding, layout, saved data and all working features. Do not rebuild the entire application.\n\n## 1. IMPROVE AI TUTOR RESPONSE SPEED\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\nThe AI Tutor takes too long to respond to student questions.\n\nInvestigate and optimise the actual AI request workflow.\n\nRequirements:\n\n* Identify the cause of unnecessary delays.\n* Prevent duplicate API requests.\n* Avoid unnecessary AI processing steps.\n* Reduce excessive conversation history while preserving relevant context for follow-up questions.\n* Use an appropriately fast AI model supported by the existing API configuration and available quota.\n* Implement streaming responses so students can see answers as they are generated, if supported by the current API.\n* Show a clean loading indicator while waiting.\n* Avoid unnecessary diagram or image generation.\n* Use lightweight SVG or CSS diagrams when appropriate.\n* Handle 429 and 503 errors properly.\n* Provide a Retry button when a request fails.\n* Preserve the student\'s original question when an error occurs.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not sacrifice explanation quality or remove conversational memory to improve speed. Do not repeatedly retry requests when the API quota has been exhausted.\n\nThe goal is to make the AI Tutor feel more responsive and reduce unnecessary waiting.\n\n## 2. ADD A CREATE NEW NOTE OPTION\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\nThe My Notes section needs a clear option for creating new notes.\n\nAdd a prominent button labelled:\n\n\"+ Create New Note\"\n\nWhen clicked, open a note editor containing:\n\n* Note title.\n* Subject or category.\n* Main text area for writing notes.\n* Save button.\n* Cancel button.\n\nAdditional functionality:\n\n* Allow students to create multiple notes.\n* Allow students to edit existing notes.\n* Allow students to delete notes with a confirmation message.\n* Automatically save changes where appropriate.\n* Display saved notes in an organised list.\n* Show the note title, subject and last-updated date.\n* Allow students to reopen and continue editing their notes.\n\nSave notes using the existing persistent storage system.\n\nNotes must remain available after refreshing the website or reopening it.\n\nMake sure creating a new note never overwrites an existing note.\n\n## 3. ADD A DELETE OPTION TO STUDY ROADMAP\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\nStudents can create study roadmaps, but they need the ability to delete schedules they no longer want.\n\nAdd a clearly visible three-dot menu or delete icon to each saved roadmap.\n\nWhen clicked, provide a Delete Roadmap option.\n\nBefore deleting, show a confirmation dialog:\n\n\"Are you sure you want to delete this study roadmap? This action cannot be undone.\"\n\nProvide two buttons:\n\n* Cancel\n* Delete Roadmap\n\nWhen the student confirms deletion:\n\n* Delete only the selected roadmap.\n* Remove its associated schedule and completion data.\n* Update the roadmap list immediately.\n* Recalculate the displayed progress using the remaining actual data.\n* If the deleted roadmap is currently open, navigate to another saved roadmap or return to the empty roadmap screen.\n* Do not delete any other roadmap.\n* Do not delete the student\'s saved AI Tutor conversations or personal notes.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe deletion must also remove the selected roadmap from persistent storage, not merely hide it from the screen.\n\nIf deletion fails, display an error message and preserve the roadmap.\n\nIf no roadmaps exist, display a clean empty state:\n\n\"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\"\n\n## 4. TEST EVERYTHING\n\nAfter implementing the changes, test these scenarios:\n\nAI TUTOR:\n\n* Ask a normal academic question.\n* Confirm the response begins appearing promptly.\n* Ask a follow-up question.\n* Confirm conversation context is preserved.\n* Test temporary API errors.\n\nMY NOTES:\n\n* Create a new note.\n* Save it.\n* Edit it.\n* Refresh the page.\n* Confirm it remains saved.\n* Create a second note and confirm the first note is not overwritten.\n\nSTUDY ROADMAP:\n\n* Create two separate roadmaps.\n* Delete one roadmap.\n* Confirm the other remains available.\n* Refresh the page.\n* Confirm the deleted roadmap does not reappear.\n\nFINAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n* Preserve all four main Study Flow features.\n* Preserve genuine student data.\n* Do not introduce fake notes, fake roadmaps or artificial progress.\n* Make every newly added button functional.\n* Keep the interface responsive on desktop, tablet and mobile.\n* Make actual code changes and test them.\n\nPrioritise reliability and functionality over unnecessary visual changes."
    }
  }
}
