  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Delete Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into Requirement 3, specifically the need to add a delete option to the study roadmap. The core issue is the lack of a straightforward way to remove saved roadmaps, which also requires an update to the progress data. I\'m considering the best UI/UX implementation and how this option should interact with and update the roadmap\'s progress data effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Delete Implementation**\n\nI\'m now honing the delete roadmap functionality. I\'ve settled on a delete icon within the roadmap item and a confirmation modal for safety. Upon confirmation, I\'ll remove the roadmap and related data from storage, update the roadmap list, recalculate progress, and handle navigation if the deleted roadmap was in view. Also, I am planning to implement the empty state.\n\n\n**Implementing Empty State Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added the empty state messaging and button for no active roadmaps. The text will be, \"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\" I\'ve also integrated the new roadmap creation button into this empty state view. Now, I\'m integrating this logic into the code and testing the result of this addition.\n\n\n**Finalizing Roadmap Deletion**\n\nI\'ve just solidified the deletion workflow. Upon deletion confirmation, I\'ll update the `roadmaps` state instantly. If roadmaps remain, I\'ll switch the `activeRoadmapId` to the first remaining one. If none are left, I\'ll clear `activeRoadmapId` and display the empty state with the message, \"No study roadmaps yet. Create your first roadmap to get started!\" and a create button. Also, I\'ll recalculate progress in StorageService based on any roadmaps remaining.\n\n\n"
