  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md"
    end_line: 99
    content: "---\nname: \"gemini-api\"\ndescription: >\n  Provides model selection guidance and coding patterns for the @google/genai\n  TypeScript SDK. Use when the application requires AI capabilities (e.g.,\n  text/image/music generation, audio transcription, smart features) or when the\n  task involves implementing an \"AI-powered\" feature. The model should prefer\n  this modern SDK over legacy alternatives. Do NOT use for general discussions\n  about AI without implementation intent. Covers model aliases, streaming, chat,\n  function calling, search and maps grounding, image generation, music\n  generation (Lyria), audio transcription, TTS, Live API, and API key handling.\n---\n\n## @google/genai Models\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> The models listed in this section are the absolute source of truth when\n> selecting a model. Even if a specific use case is not listed in the examples\n> or sections below, you must still choose one of the models defined here,\n> unless the user specifies one.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **NEVER** use the following deprecated models. They are strictly prohibited\n> and unsupported: - `gemini-1.5-flash` - `gemini-1.5-pro` - `gemini-pro` -\n> `gemini-2.0-flash` - `gemini-2.0-pro` - `gemini-2.0-flash-thinking`\n>\n> Always select a valid model from the list below.\n\n-   If the user provides a full model name that includes hyphens, a version, and\n    an optional date (e.g., gemini-2.5-flash-preview-12-2025 or\n    gemini-3.1-pro-preview), use it directly.\n-   If the user provides a common name or alias, use the following full model\n    name.\n    -   gemini flash: \'gemini-flash-latest\'\n    -   gemini 3.8 flash: \'gemini-3.8-flash\'\n    -   gemini lite or flash lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'\n    -   gemini pro, gemini 4, or gemini argon: \'gemini-4-argon\'\n    -   nano banana, or gemini flash image, or nano banana lite, or nano banana\n        2 lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   nano banana 2.1: \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   nano banana pro, or gemini pro image: \'gemini-3-pro-image\'\n    -   native audio, gemini live, or gemini flash audio: \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   gemini live extended thinking or thinker talker:\n        \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   gemini transcribe or audio transcription: \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   live transcribe or live audio transcription:\n        \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   live translate or live speech translation:\n        \'gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview\'\n    -   gemini tts, gemini text-to-speech, or gemini flash lite tts:\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   gemini flash tts: \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   gemini omni flash, Veo, or Veo lite: \'gemini-omni-1.1-flash\'\n    -   Lyria Clip: \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Lyria Pro: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n-   If the user does not specify any model, select the following model based on\n    the task type.\n    -   Basic Text Tasks (e.g., summarization, proofreading, and simple Q&A):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash\'\n    -   Complex Text Tasks (e.g., advanced reasoning, coding, math, and STEM):\n        \'gemini-4-argon\'\n    -   General Image Generation and Editing Tasks:\n        \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   High-Quality Image Generation and Editing Tasks (supports 1K, 2K, and 4K\n        resolution): \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   Video Generation, Editing, and Extension Tasks: \'gemini-omni-1.1-flash\'\n    -   Audio Transcription Tasks (pre-recorded or static audio via\n        generateContent): \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   Real-time audio & video conversation tasks (via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   Real-time voice conversation tasks requiring complex reasoning or\n        multi-step tool use (via Live API): \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   Real-time live audio transcription tasks (speech-to-text via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   Real-time speech-to-speech translation tasks (via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview\'\n    -   General Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g., article reading, global\n        dubbing/localization, customer service IVR, accessibility screen\n        readers, and high-throughput voice assistants):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   Voice Design, Screenplay, and Podcasting Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g.,\n        prompting custom voice personas from scratch, dual-speaker screenplay\n        editing, and dialogue apps requiring backchanneling like `|mhm|` or\n        `|yeah|` and vocal bursts like `<laugh>` or `<gasp>`):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   Short music clip generation tasks (30s): \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Full-length music generation tasks: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n    -   Embedding tasks: \'gemini-embedding-2-preview\'\n\nThe following models require a paid API key. Prompt the user to select one by\ncalling the `show_aistudio_ui` tool with arguments: `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"`\n*before* using these models.\n\n-   `gemini-4-argon`\n-   `gemini-3-pro-image`\n-   `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`\n-   `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`\n-   `gemini-omni-1.1-flash`"
    num_lines: 621
    num_bytes: 22720
    is_skill_file: true
    skill_metadata {
      name: "gemini-api"
      description: "Provides model selection guidance and coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Use when the application requires AI capabilities (e.g., text/image/music generation, audio transcription, smart features) or when the task involves implementing an \"AI-powered\" feature. The model should prefer this modern SDK over legacy alternatives. Do NOT use for general discussions about AI without implementation intent. Covers model aliases, streaming, chat, function calling, search and maps grounding, image generation, music generation (Lyria), audio transcription, TTS, Live API, and API key handling."
    }
    line_range_bytes: 5015
  }
