  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Task Requirements**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the first task, scrutinizing the specified model choices and their associated configurations. Specifically, I am cross-referencing the model names and settings to ensure complete alignment with all requirements. My primary focus is on `gemini-3.8-flash` with ThinkingLevel.LOW and the fallback to `gemini-3.1-flash`. I\'m verifying the model choices now.\n\n\n**Adding Note Creation Feature**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the second task. I am designing the user interface for the \"Create New Note\" feature, and making sure the note editor includes a title, subject/category, text area, save button, and cancel button. Multiple note creation is a must and I am making sure the new note doesn\'t overwrite any of the existing ones.\n\n\n**Refining Note Editor Workflow**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the note creation process. I\'ve updated the \"New Note\" button to read \"+ Create New Note\". Now, when the user clicks this, the note editor appears. The editor features a title input with a placeholder, a subject/category field (considering either a select dropdown or editable input), and a main text area. I\'m focusing on a clean design.\n\n\n**Implementing Note Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the note actions, starting with save and cancel. I am labeling the save button as \"Save\" or \"Save Note\" and the cancel button as \"Cancel\". I\'m also addressing note overwriting, and implementing logic using `isCreatingNew` and `editingNoteId`. I am generating unique IDs for new notes using the format `note-{timestamp}-{randomString}`. This ensures that new notes never overwrite existing notes.\nI\'m now turning my attention to adding a delete button with a confirmation dialog.\n\n\n**Adding Delete Functionality**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the delete functionality for the study roadmaps. My focus is on adding a visible delete option, either a dropdown or icon, to each roadmap item. I\'m prioritizing implementing a confirmation modal to avoid accidental deletions and providing a clear message within it. The roadmap data updates will be triggered after confirmation.\n\n\n**Finalizing Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the confirmation modal\'s design. The message will clearly state, \"Are you sure you want to delete this study roadmap? This action cannot be undone.\" The modal features \"Cancel\" and \"Delete Roadmap\" buttons. Upon confirmation, I\'ll remove the roadmap and related schedule/completion data from storage. I\'m also addressing UI updates, triggering a list refresh and progress recalculation. I need to preserve all other data. If nothing remains, I\'ll show an empty state message and button. I\'m checking the calculations in `src/services/storage.ts` to see what is tracked.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now examining how deleting a roadmap impacts related data. I\'m focusing on cleaning up session logs tagged with the roadmap and recalculating stats. I\'m considering using `StorageService.deleteRoadmap()` with specific filtering and updates to `localStorage`. I\'m making sure to handle the empty state, too. I\'ll make sure `ROADMAPS_KEY` stores `\"[]\"` if needed.\n\n\n**Refining Empty State Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the empty state in relation to storage. The earlier implementation was actually correct because if the `ROADMAPS_KEY` contains `\"[]\"`, that is an accurate representation of an empty roadmap list. Deleting the last roadmap does not need to reset to null, just to `\"[]\"`. The `deleteRoadmap()` function correctly handles deleting and keeping the empty state. I\'m focusing on ensuring all aspects of the application correctly interpret an empty array of roadmaps.\n\n\n**Calculating Progress Metrics**\n\nI\'m now implementing the recalculation of personal progress metrics after roadmap deletion. I\'m focusing on cleaning session logs related to the deleted roadmap. I\'m removing sessions that match the roadmap\'s title or subject. Also, I\'m recalculating total study minutes and sessions completed, ensuring they are non-negative.\n\n\n**Confirming Modal Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the modal and UI elements for the study roadmap delete function. I\'ve confirmed that the confirmation modal message and button labels are correct. I\'m focusing on adding a delete button to each roadmap card and linking its action to the modal trigger, and then making the correct updates to the UI and state based on modal confirmation.\n\n\n"
