  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Study Roadmap**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `StudyRoadmapView.tsx` component, specifically the feature to delete saved roadmaps. I need to ensure a smooth deletion process that also updates related data consistently. I am thinking about how to implement the delete option and how to handle data updates when a roadmap is deleted.\n\n\n**Implementing Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'ve outlined the core requirements for the roadmap deletion feature. I\'m focusing on the user flow, including adding a visible delete option (thinking dropdown or icon) and the crucial confirmation modal to prevent accidental data loss. I\'m also planning the data management side, including updating storage and recalculating progress when a roadmap is deleted. I need to make sure the student will be navigated away from the deleted roadmap, and a good message is provided if this is the last roadmap.\n\n\n**Designing Delete Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI/UX elements for roadmap deletion in `mapView.tsx`. I\'ve detailed the `roadmapToDelete` state. The confirmation modal will use the precise message and button labels as specified. I plan to add the delete icon button and its tooltip to the roadmap switcher and summary banner. Deletion will call `StorageService.deleteRoadmap`, which also cleans up progress logs, and then update the roadmap list.\n\n\n"
