    thinking: "**Adding Delete Button Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a plan to add the delete button functionality in `StudyRoadmapView.tsx`. When there are roadmaps to work with, next to the `<select>` element, I\'ll incorporate a delete button that triggers `setRoadmapToDelete(activeRoadmap)`. This button\'s going to be styled with the `p-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-9` class.\n\n\n**Implementing Delete Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the actual delete features. The plan is to have a button with the trash icon next to the roadmap title. This button will call `setRoadmapToDelete(activeRoadmap)`. I\'ve also added a delete confirmation modal. It will show when `roadmapToDelete` is set, and it includes a warning. I\'ll need to figure out how to update the roadmap manager / pills or list to also have delete functionality.\n\n\n**Refining Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'ve been refining the delete confirmation modal. It\'s now showing the roadmap title with the text \"Delete Study Roadmap,\" below that. Then, I\'ve added a warning message that this action cannot be undone. I\'m focusing now on the layout and functionality of the confirm/cancel buttons.\n\n\n**Designing Empty State UI**\n\nI\'m now designing the empty state UI. When there are no roadmaps and we aren\'t creating a new one, I\'m thinking of displaying a centered, rounded container with an icon and a message. The container will feature a compass icon, and a call to action button to start creating roadmaps. It\'s designed to be clear and visually appealing.\n\n\n"
